l":"/en/docs/guide-loader#handles","content":"`options()`","locale":"en"},"6395":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-100","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#handles","content":"the current options","locale":"en"},"6396":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-101","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#handles","content":"`inner_fiber()`, `outer_fiber()`","locale":"en"},"6397":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-102","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#handles","content":"the plugin's fiber, and the fiber holding `inject` (if any)","locale":"en"},"6398":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-103","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#handles","content":"`is_disabled()`","locale":"en"},"6399":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-104","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#handles","content":"whether the entry is, or reads as, disabled, including through its ancestors","locale":"en"},"6400":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-105","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#handles","content":"`parent()`, `subgroup()`, `subtree()`","locale":"en"},"6401":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-106","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#handles","content":"its group, and the group or tree its plugin owns","locale":"en"},"6402":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-107","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#handles","content":"`init().await`","locale":"en"},"6403":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-108","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#handles","content":"starts the entry if it is not running, or joins its pending start","locale":"en"},"6404":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-109","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"**`create(options, parent, position)`** validates the options deeply (including a group's members) before anything is committed, assigns an id if there is none, inserts the entry at `position` (clamped; `None` appends) in the group of entry `parent` (`None` for the root group) and starts it. A group entry creates its group when its plugin loads, so a `parent` that is still loading is awaited. (Entries that come from a file or a group update are validated shallowly instead, each group member when its group reconciles it; `kardia_loader::validate_options(&options, deep)` is the check.)","locale":"en"},"6405":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-110","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"**`update(id, patch, parent, position)`** merges `patch` into the options (`null` deletes a key), validates the result and applies it. `parent: None` leaves the entry where it is; `Some(None)` moves it to the root group and `Some(Some(id))` into the group of entry `id`, also across trees: a move into another tree takes the entry's group members along and fails if one of their ids already exists there.","locale":"en"},"6406":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-111","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"What an update does to the running plugin depends on what changed:","locale":"en"},"6407":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-112","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"a changed `name` or `inject`, or an entry that is not running: the entry is rebuilt (its fibers disposed, then started again);","locale":"en"},"6408":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-113","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"otherwise the running fibers are patched in place: the entry is re-attached under its (new) group with its new isolation table (re-attaching an entry's context also moves every fiber below it, as with a re-pointed JavaScript prototype), `intercept` is swapped in place, and a changed `config` reaches the plugin as `fiber.update_with(config, true)`, which the plugin's update hook may take over instead of restarting.","locale":"en"},"6409":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-114","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"**`remove(id)`** disposes the entry and removes it from its group.","locale":"en"},"6410":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-115","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"**Write-back.** Changes a plugin makes to itself reach its entry:","locale":"en"},"6411":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-116","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"a plugin that disposes itself is persisted as `disabled: true`;","locale":"en"},"6412":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-117","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"a plugin that updates its own configuration (`fiber.update(..)`, which emits `ConfigCommitted`) has the new `config` written to its entry;","locale":"en"},"6413":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-118","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"a dependency loss unloads an entry's outer fiber without disposing it; the entry then reads as disabled until its outer fiber is reactivated, and nothing is written.","locale":"en"},"6414":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-119","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"Every change applied to a tree is reported to its backend as an `EntryChange`, after it has been applied:","locale":"en"},"6415":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-120","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"`EntryChange` fields","locale":"en"},"6416":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-121","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"6417":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-122","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"`id`, `group`","locale":"en"},"6418":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-123","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"the entry's local id and the group it is now in","locale":"en"},"6419":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-124","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"`options` absent","locale":"en"},"6420":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-125","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"the entry was removed from `group`","locale":"en"},"6421":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-126","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"`legacy` absent","locale":"en"},"6422":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-127","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"the entry was created in `group`","locale":"en"},"6423":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-128","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"both present","locale":"en"},"6424":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-129","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"the entry was updated; `from` is the group it left if it moved within the tree","locale":"en"},"6425":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-130","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#crud","content":"A move into another tree is reported as a removal from the source tree and a creation in the target.","locale":"en"},"6426":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-131","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"A `TreeBackend` decides where a tree's changes go. Every method has a default:","locale":"en"},"6427":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-132","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"`TreeBackend` method","locale":"en"},"6428":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-133","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"Default","locale":"en"},"6429":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-134","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"Purpose","locale":"en"},"6430":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-135","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"`commit(&change)`","locale":"en"},"6431":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-136","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"nothing","locale":"en"},"6432":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-137","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"called synchronously after a change has been applied to the tree","locale":"en"},"6433":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-138","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"`resolver()`","locale":"en"},"6434":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-139","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"`None` (the loader's resolver)","locale":"en"},"6435":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-140","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"resolves plugin names for this tree","locale":"en"},"6436":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-141","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"`base_dir()`","locale":"en"},"6437":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-142","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"`None`","locale":"en"},"6438":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-143","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"the directory relative paths inside this tree resolve against","locale":"en"},"6439":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-144","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"`handle()`","locale":"en"},"6440":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-145","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"`None`","locale":"en"},"6441":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-146","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"the object behind the tree, for its owner to find it again","locale":"en"},"6442":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-147","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"`locate(id, path, value)`","locale":"en"},"6443":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-148","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"`None`","locale":"en"},"6444":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-149","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"where the value at `path` in the options of entry `id` is written; with `value`, only if that is the value written there; without, a missing value is located at its closest written ancestor","locale":"en"},"6445":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-150","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"`locate_expr(id, path, expr, offset)`","locale":"en"},"6446":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-151","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"`None`","locale":"en"},"6447":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-152","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#backends","content":"where char `offset` of the expression `expr` at `path` is written","locale":"en"},"6448":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-153","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#isolation","content":"Entries set up isolation and interception declaratively.","locale":"en"},"6449":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-154","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#isolation","content":"**`isolate`** gives the entry's services their own realm:","locale":"en"},"6450":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-155","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#isolation","content":"`isolate: { db: true }` makes `db` private to the entry;","locale":"en"},"6451":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-156","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#isolation","content":"`isolate: { db: shared }` puts `db` into a realm shared by every entry using the label `shared`.","locale":"en"},"6452":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-157","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#isolation","content":"(The TypeScript loader names these realms `db#<id>` and `db@shared`; in kardia they are plain `RealmId`s, which print as `realm#<n>`.)","locale":"en"},"6453":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-158","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#isolation","content":"When an entry's effective realms change (a new `isolate`, or a move to another group), a binding provided from inside the entry **migrates** to the new realm without restarting its provider, as long as the new realm is free; the consumers of both realms re-resolve. A shared realm is released once no entry uses its label for that service any more.","locale":"en"},"6454":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-159","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#isolation","content":"**`intercept`** is metadata for the services the entry's plugin uses, keyed by service: `intercept: { logger: { name: db, level: 3 } }`. It is evaluated (it may contain expressions) and swapped in place, so a running plugin sees new metadata without a restart. A failing `intercept` disables the entry.","locale":"en"},"6455":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-160","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#isolation","content":"**`inject`** as a map attaches metadata to a declared dependency: `inject: { loader: { await: true } }`. The metadata may contain expressions, evaluated in the parent group's context; a failure disables the entry.","locale":"en"},"6456":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-161","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include","content":"The `include` plugin (`kardia_include::IncludePlugin`) loads the entries of a YAML or JSON file as a subtree and keeps the file in sync both ways. It declares the `loader` service; with `watch` it also needs `fs`.","locale":"en"},"6457":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-162","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include","content":"Option","locale":"en"},"6458":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-163","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"6459":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-164","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include","content":"`path`","locale":"en"},"6460":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-165","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include","content":"the file, relative to the base directory of the tree the include entry is in (for a nested include, the directory of the including file); `.json`, `.yaml` or `.yml`","locale":"en"},"6461":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-166","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include","content":"`watch`","locale":"en"},"6462":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-167","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include","content":"re-read the file whenever it changes (needs the `fs` service)","locale":"en"},"6463":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-168","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include","content":"`initial`","locale":"en"},"6464":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-169","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include","content":"entries written to the file if it does not exist yet","locale":"en"},"6465":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-170","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include","content":"`patches`","locale":"en"},"6466":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-171","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include","content":"overrides and additions applied on top of the file (below)","locale":"en"},"6467":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-172","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include","content":"**Starting.** The include reads the file. If the file is missing and `initial` is set, it writes `initial` (with ids assigned) and reads that; without `initial` it fails with `config file not found: <path>`. Any other read, parse or validation failure fails the plugin, as does an unsupported extension (`extension \"toml\" not supported`). A file must be a top-level array of objects.","locale":"en"},"6468":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-173","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include","content":"**File edits → tree.** Each read is reconciled into the subtree; only the latest intended tree is applied, older ones are skipped. A file that fails to parse mid-edit (an empty or truncated file is routine while editing) is logged as a warning, the running tree stays as it was, and nothing is written until a later read succeeds.","locale":"en"},"6469":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-174","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include","content":"**Tree changes → file.** Runtime changes of the subtree (API edits, plugin self-updates and self-disposals) are recorded in a journal and written back to whoever owns them: the file, or a patch in the include's own configuration, which is persisted through the include's own entry in the parent tree. Shutting down does not write to the file.","locale":"en"},"6470":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-175","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include","content":"**Anonymous entries.** Entries the file leaves without an id get one before the loader sees them, and the id is written back. An anonymous entry that looks exactly like one from the previous read keeps that id (unless the file now names it explicitly), so editing a neighbour does not restart it.","locale":"en"},"6471":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-176","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#patches","content":"`patches` let a parent file adjust an included file without editing it:","locale":"en"},"6472":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-177","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#patches","content":"Patch","locale":"en"},"6473":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-178","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#patches","content":"Effect","locale":"en"},"6474":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-179","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#patches","content":"`{ insert: [..] }`","locale":"en"},"6475":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-180","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#patches","content":"appends entries to the included root","locale":"en"},"6476":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-181","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#patches","content":"`{ id, insert: [..] }`","locale":"en"},"6477":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-182","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#patches","content":"appends entries to the group `id`","locale":"en"},"6478":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-183","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#patches","content":"`{ id, name?, ..keys }`","locale":"en"},"6479":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-184","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#patches","content":"overrides keys of entry `id`","locale":"en"},"6480":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-185","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#patches","content":"A patch that does not apply (`patch insert: entry x not found`, `… is not a group`) is reported as a warning and owns nothing. Every inserted entry gets an id, so that runtime changes can be routed back to it. The include tracks who supplies each entry and key (the file, a patch overriding a key, or an entry written inside a patch), and writes a runtime change of a patch-owned value into the patch, not the file. New `patches` are applied in place when the include's configuration is updated; a different `path` or `watch` restarts it.","locale":"en"},"6481":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-186","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#writes","content":"**Atomic writes.** The include writes a temp file in the same directory (`.<name>.<pid>.<seq>.tmp`) and renames it over the file, so no reader sees a truncated file.","locale":"en"},"6482":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-187","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#writes","content":"**Stale-content check.** Before every rename, it checks that the file still holds the content it last read. If someone else wrote the file meanwhile, it reads and merges first, then writes again.","locale":"en"},"6483":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-188","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#writes","content":"**Transient failures.** A rename that fails with `PermissionDenied` or `ResourceBusy` (such as a virus scanner holding the file) is retried up to 10 times, waiting 20 ms longer each time.","locale":"en"},"6484":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-189","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#writes","content":"**Read-only or missing files.** Changes are kept in memory, with a warning: `config file <path> is read-only, N pending change(s) kept in memory` (or `is missing`). A failed write logs `failed to write config file <path>, N pending change(s) kept in memory`.","locale":"en"},"6485":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-190","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#writes","content":"**Conflicts: the file wins.** When the file changes while runtime changes are pending, the include merges three ways. Conflicting runtime changes are dropped so that the tree follows the file, and each drop is logged as `config conflict in <path>: entry <id> <reason>; file wins`, with one of these reasons:","locale":"en"},"6486":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-191","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#writes","content":"`key \"k\" modified both in file and at runtime`","locale":"en"},"6487":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-192","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#writes","content":"`removed in file, modified at runtime`","locale":"en"},"6488":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-193","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#writes","content":"`modified in file, removed at runtime`","locale":"en"},"6489":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-194","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#writes","content":"`added in file, removed at runtime`","locale":"en"},"6490":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-195","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#writes","content":"`moved both in file and at runtime`","locale":"en"},"6491":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-196","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include-api","content":"`Include::of(&tree)` returns the running include behind a tree it created:","locale":"en"},"6492":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-197","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include-api","content":"Method","locale":"en"},"6493":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-198","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include-api","content":"Does","locale":"en"},"6494":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-199","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include-api","content":"`include.filename()`","locale":"en"},"6495":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-200","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include-api","content":"the absolute path of the file","locale":"en"},"6496":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-201","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include-api","content":"`include.tree()`","locale":"en"},"6497":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-202","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include-api","content":"its `TreeHandle`","locale":"en"},"6498":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-203","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include-api","content":"`include.refresh().await`","locale":"en"},"6499":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-204","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include-api","content":"re-reads the file and reconciles the tree with it (what a watcher triggers), then waits for every pending read and write","locale":"en"},"6500":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-205","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include-api","content":"`include.flush().await`","locale":"en"},"6501":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-206","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include-api","content":"resolves once every pending read and write has been processed and the tree reflects the outcome","locale":"en"},"6502":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-207","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include-api","content":"`include.stop().await`","locale":"en"},"6503":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-208","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include-api","content":"flushes what the user last did, then removes the tree's entries","locale":"en"},"6504":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-209","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include-api","content":"`IncludePlugin::with_rename(rename)` is the plugin with a custom rename function in place of `std::fs::rename`, for fault-injection tests.","locale":"en"},"6505":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-210","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#include-api","content":"In YAML, `!!js <source>` reads as an expression object `{ \"__jsExpr\": source }` and is written back the same way. Unknown tags are errors, since they would leave the data incomplete. Written YAML uses block style, with single-quoted strings where needed.","locale":"en"},"6506":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-211","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#errors","content":"Errors in config files point at the place they refer to, as `file:line:col`.","locale":"en"},"6507":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-212","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#errors","content":"**Read, parse and validation errors** of a file are a `ConfigFileError { stage, path, cause, issues }`:","locale":"en"},"6508":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-213","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#errors","content":"The first line names the stage (`read`, `parse` or `validate`) and, for a read failure, its cause; each issue follows with its position.","locale":"en"},"6509":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-214","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#errors","content":"**Entry errors** the loader logs (option and config validation, `ModuleNotFound`, expression failures) are located through the tree backend's `locate` / `locate_expr`. Each issue gets `(at <path>, file:line:col)`, an expression failure an `at <path> (file:line:col)` frame, and the entry and each ancestor that has a position an `at <id> (file:line:col)` frame:","locale":"en"},"6510":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-215","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#errors","content":"How values are located:","locale":"en"},"6511":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-216","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#errors","content":"the include locates a value where its owner writes it: in its file, or in a patch in its parent's file;","locale":"en"},"6512":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-217","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#errors","content":"a YAML alias is located at its anchor;","locale":"en"},"6513":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-218","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#errors","content":"a char of an expression is located through YAML escapes;","locale":"en"},"6514":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-219","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#errors","content":"a missing value is located at the key that should hold it (its closest written ancestor);","locale":"en"},"6515":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-220","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#errors","content":"a JSON file is located by parsing it as YAML as well (JSON is YAML), so it gets the same positions;","locale":"en"},"6516":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-221","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#errors","content":"values changed at runtime are not located, and an error that cannot be located at all is logged as it is.","locale":"en"},"6517":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-222","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#errors","content":"The loader does not expose an `Entry::evaluate` for evaluating expressions of an entry from outside.","locale":"en"},"6518":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-223","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#errors","content":"A custom `TreeBackend` gets the same output by implementing `locate` and `locate_expr`; `TreeHandle::locate` and `TreeHandle::locate_expr` call them for a local id.","locale":"en"},"6519":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-224","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#patch-context","content":"The loader patches an entry's context when the entry starts and when its options change in place: it re-attaches the context under its group, installs the isolation table and reconciles the running fibers. `loader.on_patch_context(ctx, hook)` wraps that step (the TypeScript `loader/patch-context` waterfall):","locale":"en"},"6520":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-225","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#patch-context","content":"The hook gets the entry and `next`, the rest of the chain as a future. `next` builds the rest only when it is awaited, so a hook runs after the ones registered before it, and a hook that does not await `next` stops the later hooks and the patch.","locale":"en"},"6521":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-226","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#patch-context","content":"Hooks run in registration order, inside the loader's own isolation step.","locale":"en"},"6522":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-227","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#patch-context","content":"The registration is an effect of `ctx`'s fiber, so the hook is removed with it.","locale":"en"},"6523":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-228","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#patch-context","content":"Unlike the TypeScript loader, the new isolation table is installed together with the re-parenting at the end of the chain, not before the hooks run.","locale":"en"},"6524":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-loader-229","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-loader#patch-context","content":"`EntryHandle::init().await` starts an entry if it is not running, or joins its pending start; concurrent callers share one start.","locale":"en"},"6525":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"page","content":"Writing plugins","breadcrumbs":["kardia Documentation","Guide"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","locale":"en"},"6526":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","content":"Services and plugins in Rust: #[derive(Service)], #[plugin], the Plugin trait, PluginDef, and registering plugins for the loader.","locale":"en"},"6527":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#add-the-dependency","content":"Add the dependency","locale":"en"},"6528":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#a-first-example","content":"A first example","locale":"en"},"6529":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#services","content":"Services","locale":"en"},"6530":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#providing-a-service","content":"Providing a service","locale":"en"},"6531":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#services-for-expressions","content":"Services for expressions","locale":"en"},"6532":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#using-a-service","content":"Using a service","locale":"en"},"6533":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugins","content":"Plugins","locale":"en"},"6534":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-macro","content":"`#[plugin]` on an async function","locale":"en"},"6535":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-trait","content":"Implementing `Plugin`","locale":"en"},"6536":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-10","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#inject","content":"`Inject`","locale":"en"},"6537":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#plugin-def","content":"`PluginDef`: plugins from closures","locale":"en"},"6538":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#ctx-inject","content":"`ctx.inject`: an anonymous plugin","locale":"en"},"6539":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#starting-plugins","content":"Starting plugins","locale":"en"},"6540":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-14","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"The `Fiber` handle","locale":"en"},"6541":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-15","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#configuration","content":"Configuration","locale":"en"},"6542":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-16","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#stopping-cleanly","content":"Stopping cleanly","locale":"en"},"6543":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-17","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#loading-your-plugins-from-a-config-file","content":"Loading your plugins from a config file","locale":"en"},"6544":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#next","content":"Next","locale":"en"},"6545":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","content":"Plugins written in Rust are compiled into your app. This page shows how to declare services, write plugins that provide and use them, start them, and make them available to config files. Why the API looks this way is explained on API design.","locale":"en"},"6546":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#add-the-dependency","content":"`use kardia::prelude::*;` brings in the names most plugins need: `Context`, `Plugin`, `PluginDef`, `Inject`, `Injected`, `Service`, `Svc`, `Fiber`, `Result`, the two macros, the timer, `Loader`, `Deserialize` and `json!`.","locale":"en"},"6547":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-21","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#a-first-example","content":"Services are plain types. The `#[plugin]` macro reads a plugin's dependencies from its signature, so accessing a service it did not declare is a compile error:","locale":"en"},"6548":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-22","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#a-first-example","content":"What happens:","locale":"en"},"6549":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#a-first-example","content":"`greeter` declares `database` and `timer`. It stays pending until both are available.","locale":"en"},"6550":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-24","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#a-first-example","content":"`db` provides `database`, so `greeter` starts.","locale":"en"},"6551":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-25","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#a-first-example","content":"Updating `db`'s config restarts it. `greeter` depends on it, so `greeter` stops first and starts again with the new database.","locale":"en"},"6552":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-26","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#a-first-example","content":"Disposing `db` withdraws `database`: `greeter` stops, and its interval and the `closing` log line are reverted and run as part of the teardown.","locale":"en"},"6553":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-27","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#a-first-example","content":"A longer, runnable version, which also hot-replaces the database implementation:","locale":"en"},"6554":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-28","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#a-first-example","content":"With the facade crate `kardia`, both macros take `crate = ::kardia`. The generated code refers to `::kardia_core` by default, which only works if you depend on `kardia-core` directly.","locale":"en"},"6555":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-29","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#services","content":"A service is any `Send + Sync + 'static` type bound to a **key**, a string. Keys are strings rather than type ids because config files name services.","locale":"en"},"6556":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-30","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#services","content":"`#[derive(Service)]` uses the type name, hyphenated, as the key unless `name` is given. The `Service` trait has one more item, `merge_intercept`, which merges interception metadata; its default (a right-biased shallow merge of JSON objects) suits most services. See Services.","locale":"en"},"6557":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-31","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#providing-a-service","content":"A plugin provides a service from its `apply`:","locale":"en"},"6558":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-32","page_id":