"/en/docs/guide-plugins-117","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#starting-plugins","content":"Each returns a `Fiber`, the handle to that running instance. Starting a plugin is itself an effect of the calling plugin, so a child stops when its parent stops. Stopping the root (`root.fiber().dispose().await`) reverts everything.","locale":"en"},"6644":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-118","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"The fiber handle offers:","locale":"en"},"6645":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-119","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"Method","locale":"en"},"6646":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-120","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"Does","locale":"en"},"6647":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-121","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"`state()`","locale":"en"},"6648":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-122","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"`Pending` (waiting for dependencies), `Loading`, `Active`, `Unloading`, `Failed` or `Disposed`","locale":"en"},"6649":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-123","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"`settled().await`","locale":"en"},"6650":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-124","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"Waits until no transition is in flight; fails with the plugin's error","locale":"en"},"6651":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-125","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"`update(value)?.await`","locale":"en"},"6652":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-126","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"Replaces the configuration (below)","locale":"en"},"6653":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-127","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"`update_with(value, no_save)`","locale":"en"},"6654":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-128","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"The same; `no_save: true` skips the write-back to a config file","locale":"en"},"6655":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-129","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"`restart().await`","locale":"en"},"6656":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-130","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"Unloads and loads the plugin again","locale":"en"},"6657":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-131","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"`dispose().await`","locale":"en"},"6658":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-132","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"Stops the plugin and removes it","locale":"en"},"6659":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-133","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"`error()`","locale":"en"},"6660":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-134","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"The error of the last failed load","locale":"en"},"6661":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-135","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"`context()`, `config()`, `name()`, `parent()`, `effects()`","locale":"en"},"6662":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-136","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"Introspection","locale":"en"},"6663":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-137","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#fiber-handle","content":"A `Failed` plugin recovers only through `update`, `restart` or a replacement.","locale":"en"},"6664":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-138","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#configuration","content":"The configuration enters as JSON (from a config file, `plugin_value` or `update`) and is decoded once per load into `Config`, with serde:","locale":"en"},"6665":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-139","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#configuration","content":"A decoding error names the failing path, such as `invalid config: … (at items.1)`.","locale":"en"},"6666":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-140","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#configuration","content":"Unknown fields are tolerated, unless the config type opts into `#[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]`.","locale":"en"},"6667":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-141","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#configuration","content":"A missing configuration (`null`) is read as an empty object, so a config type whose fields all have defaults (`#[serde(default)]`) accepts it. `()` accepts anything.","locale":"en"},"6668":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-142","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#configuration","content":"`fiber.update(value)` validates the new configuration first: a rejected configuration leaves the running instance untouched. The new configuration is then offered to the plugin's update hooks. If no hook takes it over, the plugin restarts.","locale":"en"},"6669":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-143","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#configuration","content":"`ctx.on_update_with` does the same with a hook that returns the future `update` should wait for. A hook is an effect, so it goes away with the plugin.","locale":"en"},"6670":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-144","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#stopping-cleanly","content":"Everything a plugin registers through its context is an effect that is reverted when it stops: provided services, listeners, timers, child plugins, and plain disposers such as `ctx.on_dispose(…)`. Effects covers effects in full; two points matter while writing `apply`:","locale":"en"},"6671":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-145","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#stopping-cleanly","content":"**Register the inverse right after acquiring a resource**, so that nothing leaks if the plugin is stopped while starting.","locale":"en"},"6672":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-146","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#stopping-cleanly","content":"**`ctx.checkpoint()?`** is a point where a superseded load stops. It returns `Err(Interrupted)` when the plugin's target changed since the load began (it was updated, disposed or lost a dependency). Returning that error from `apply` is not a failure: the plugin unloads what it registered so far. kardia never cancels a running `apply` by itself.","locale":"en"},"6673":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-147","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#loading-your-plugins-from-a-config-file","content":"The loader resolves the `name` of each entry. To load your own plugins from a config file, register them in a `kardia::loader::Catalog` and pass it to `Loader::plugin`:","locale":"en"},"6674":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-148","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#loading-your-plugins-from-a-config-file","content":"`kardia::catalog()` holds every built-in plugin except `hmr` (which needs a module graph, see Hot reload), under its name and its TypeScript package name; `kardia::loader::builtins()` holds only `group`.","locale":"en"},"6675":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-149","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#loading-your-plugins-from-a-config-file","content":"An entry name that is not in the catalog fails with `ModuleNotFound`, located at the entry's `name`.","locale":"en"},"6676":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-150","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#loading-your-plugins-from-a-config-file","content":"`Loader::plugin` takes any `kardia::loader::Resolver`; `Catalog` is one. The `kardia` binary uses its own resolver that falls back to guest modules for names that are not built-in plugins: `crates/kardia/src/main.rs` shows the full setup, including `hmr`.","locale":"en"},"6677":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-151","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#next","content":"<Card title=\"Services\" href=\"/docs/guide-services\" description=\"Caller attribution, interception, events and the logger.\" />","locale":"en"},"6678":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-152","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#next","content":"<Card title=\"Effects\" href=\"/docs/guide-effects\" description=\"Effects, disposers, effect scopes and teardown.\" />","locale":"en"},"6679":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-153","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#next","content":"<Card title=\"Loader\" href=\"/docs/guide-loader\" description=\"Entries, groups, isolation and include from Rust.\" />","locale":"en"},"6680":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins-154","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-plugins","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-plugins#next","content":"<Card title=\"API design\" href=\"/docs/development-design\" description=\"Why the plugin API looks the way it does.\" />","locale":"en"},"6681":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"page","content":"Services, events and logging","breadcrumbs":["kardia Documentation","Guide"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services","locale":"en"},"6682":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services","content":"Provide and consume services, attribute calls to their caller, isolate and intercept services, dispatch events and log.","locale":"en"},"6683":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#defining","content":"Defining a service","locale":"en"},"6684":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"Providing a service","locale":"en"},"6685":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"Declaring dependencies","locale":"en"},"6686":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"Accessing services","locale":"en"},"6687":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#injected","content":"Compile-time checked access","locale":"en"},"6688":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"`Svc<T>` and the caller","locale":"en"},"6689":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#interception","content":"Interception metadata","locale":"en"},"6690":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"Isolation","locale":"en"},"6691":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"Events","locale":"en"},"6692":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-10","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#listening","content":"Listening","locale":"en"},"6693":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"Dispatching","locale":"en"},"6694":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"Built-in events","locale":"en"},"6695":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#hooks","content":"Hooks","locale":"en"},"6696":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-14","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#logging","content":"Logging","locale":"en"},"6697":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-15","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#exporters","content":"Exporters","locale":"en"},"6698":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-16","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-services#example","content":"A complete example","locale":"en"},"6699":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-17","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services","content":"A **service** is a value that one plugin provides and other plugins depend on. The runtime tracks who provides what and who depends on what: a plugin that declares a service starts once the service is available, restarts when it is replaced, and stops when it goes away. This page shows how to define, provide and consume services, how calls are attributed to their caller, how isolation and interception change what a context sees, and how to use events and the logger.","locale":"en"},"6700":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services","content":"For the theory behind services see Reactive coeffects; for why the Rust API looks the way it does (string keys, `Svc<T>`, no `Proxy`) see API design; every place where kardia behaves differently from the TypeScript Cordis is listed on Status and deviations.","locale":"en"},"6701":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#defining","content":"A service is any `Send + Sync + 'static` type bound to a **key** through the `Service` trait:","locale":"en"},"6702":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#defining","content":"Keys are strings because configuration files name services (`inject: [database]`). The runtime stores each value together with its type, so a key reached with the wrong Rust type fails with `AccessError::TypeMismatch` instead of being misread.","locale":"en"},"6703":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-21","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#defining","content":"Usually you derive the trait:","locale":"en"},"6704":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-22","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#defining","content":"Without `name`, the key is the type name hyphenated: `Database` → `database`, `FooBar` → `foo-bar`. `#[service(crate = …)]` points the generated code at `::kardia`; without it, it refers to `::kardia_core`.","locale":"en"},"6705":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#defining","content":"**Associated services.** Cordis's `foo.bar` associated services and `ctx.mixin` are JavaScript-object conveniences. In kardia a service named `foo.bar` is just another key. To \"extend\" another plugin's type, use an extension trait (compile time, see `Svc<T>` and the caller) or a registry service built on `kardia_core::IdTable` (run time). No accessor or mixin layer is ported.","locale":"en"},"6706":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-24","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"Providing is an **effect** of the current fiber: it is reverted when the fiber unloads (see Revertible effects). Every method returns `Result<EffectHandle>`.","locale":"en"},"6707":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-25","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"Method","locale":"en"},"6708":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-26","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"Provides","locale":"en"},"6709":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-27","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"`ctx.provide(value)`","locale":"en"},"6710":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-28","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"a `Service` under `S::NAME`","locale":"en"},"6711":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-29","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"`ctx.provide_arc(arc)`","locale":"en"},"6712":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-30","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"an `Arc<S>` you already hold","locale":"en"},"6713":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-31","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"`ctx.provide_as(key, value)`","locale":"en"},"6714":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-32","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"any `Send + Sync` value under an explicit key","locale":"en"},"6715":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-33","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"`ctx.provide_arc_as(key, arc)`","locale":"en"},"6716":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-34","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"the same, from an `Arc`","locale":"en"},"6717":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-35","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"`ctx.provide_checked(key, arc, check)`","locale":"en"},"6718":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-36","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"a value whose availability also depends on a predicate `check`, evaluated per consumer with the consumer's interception metadata. The predicate runs under the runtime lock and must not call into the runtime.","locale":"en"},"6719":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-37","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"`ctx.provide_serialized_as(key, value)`","locale":"en"},"6720":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-38","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"a `Serialize` value that also has a **JSON view**, readable with `ctx.view(key)`, by loader expressions and by guest plugins. A `serde_json::Value` provided under a key (`provide_as`, `provide_arc_as`, `provide_checked`) is its own JSON view.","locale":"en"},"6721":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-39","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"What providing does:","locale":"en"},"6722":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-40","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"**One binding per key and realm.** A second provider in the same realm fails with `KardiaError::AlreadyProvided`, whose message is `service \"database\" has been registered at <db>` (the name of the providing plugin).","locale":"en"},"6723":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-41","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"**Notification follows the provider's state.** Consumers are notified at once only if the providing fiber is `Active`; otherwise they are notified when it becomes `Active`. When the provider leaves `Active`, its consumers are notified before any of its inverses run.","locale":"en"},"6724":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-42","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"**Withdrawal waits for consumers.** Reverting the provision removes the binding and notifies the realm, then waits until every consumer that committed to this binding has finished its own cleanup, and only then removes the provision.","locale":"en"},"6725":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-43","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"**A retired provider frees its realm at once.** Disposing a provider unbinds its live provisions immediately, so a successor can provide in the same realm while the old consumers still drain (they keep reading the old binding through their committed views).","locale":"en"},"6726":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-44","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"**A stale load cannot provide.** A retired fiber whose load is still in flight may still register inverses (so nothing it acquired leaks), but its `provide` calls fail with `KardiaError::InactiveEffect`.","locale":"en"},"6727":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-45","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"**Removal is postponed during a drain.** While a provider is unloading, its withdrawn provisions stay reachable to its descendants until the drain ends, so they can use inherited services during their own cleanup.","locale":"en"},"6728":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-46","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"`.provides([..])` on a `PluginDef` (or `provide = [..]` in `#[plugin]`, or `Plugin::provide()`) only **declares** what a plugin provides. The declaration is metadata for tooling and for the dependency-cycle check; a plugin can provide undeclared keys, which simply escape the check.","locale":"en"},"6729":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-47","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#providing","content":"There is no in-place overwrite of a bound value. To change what consumers see, provide a new value (withdraw and re-provide, restart or update the provider), so that the change is observed.","locale":"en"},"6730":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-48","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"A plugin lists the services it needs in its **inject** declaration, an `Inject`: ordered keys, each with optional interception metadata.","locale":"en"},"6731":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-49","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"Where the declaration goes:","locale":"en"},"6732":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-50","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"Plugin form","locale":"en"},"6733":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-51","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"Declaration","locale":"en"},"6734":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-52","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"`impl Plugin for P`","locale":"en"},"6735":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-53","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"`fn inject() -> Inject`","locale":"en"},"6736":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-54","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"`#[plugin]` function","locale":"en"},"6737":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-55","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"the type of its context parameter, `Injected<(A, B)>`","locale":"en"},"6738":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-56","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"`PluginDef::new` / `PluginDef::typed`","locale":"en"},"6739":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-57","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"`.inject(..)`","locale":"en"},"6740":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-58","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"a closure plugin","locale":"en"},"6741":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-59","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"`ctx.inject(deps, \\|ctx\\| async move { … })`","locale":"en"},"6742":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-60","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"a loader entry","locale":"en"},"6743":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-61","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"its `inject` field (see Configuration)","locale":"en"},"6744":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-62","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"The runtime keeps the fiber in step with its declaration:","locale":"en"},"6745":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-63","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"It stays `Pending` until every declared service is available, then loads.","locale":"en"},"6746":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-64","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"If a declared service is replaced by another binding, it unloads and loads again against the new one.","locale":"en"},"6747":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-65","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"If a declared service goes away, it unloads and waits in `Pending`.","locale":"en"},"6748":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-66","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#declaring","content":"**Dependency cycles.** When a fiber is inserted, the runtime checks whether the declared `provide` and `inject` sets of the live fibers in its realm form a cycle through it. If they do, it logs a warning naming the cycle (`dependency cycle: a -> b -> a`) and the fiber stays `Pending`, instead of waiting silently.","locale":"en"},"6749":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-67","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"Method","locale":"en"},"6750":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-68","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"Returns","locale":"en"},"6751":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-69","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"Access","locale":"en"},"6752":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-70","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`ctx.get::<S>()`","locale":"en"},"6753":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-71","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`Result<Svc<S>, AccessError>`","locale":"en"},"6754":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-72","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"checked, through committed views","locale":"en"},"6755":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-73","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`ctx.get_as::<T>(key)`","locale":"en"},"6756":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-74","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`Result<Svc<T>, AccessError>`","locale":"en"},"6757":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-75","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"checked, by key, for any type","locale":"en"},"6758":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-76","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`ctx.view(key)`","locale":"en"},"6759":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-77","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`Result<Value, AccessError>`","locale":"en"},"6760":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-78","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"checked, the service's JSON view","locale":"en"},"6761":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-79","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`ctx.deps::<(A, B)>()`","locale":"en"},"6762":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-80","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`Result<(Svc<A>, Svc<B>), AccessError>`","locale":"en"},"6763":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-81","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"checked, a tuple of up to eight services","locale":"en"},"6764":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-82","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`ctx.live::<S>()`","locale":"en"},"6765":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-83","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`Option<Svc<S>>`","locale":"en"},"6766":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-84","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"reflective: the live binding of the realm, if its provider is active; never fails for undeclared keys","locale":"en"},"6767":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-85","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`ctx.live_as::<T>(key)`","locale":"en"},"6768":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-86","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`Option<Svc<T>>`","locale":"en"},"6769":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-87","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"the same, by key","locale":"en"},"6770":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-88","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"**Checked access** (the paper's Algorithm 6) resolves a key like this:","locale":"en"},"6771":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-89","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"A binding that a fiber on the way provides itself, in the same realm, is returned directly.","locale":"en"},"6772":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-90","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"Otherwise the walk goes up through the fibers that derived the context.","locale":"en"},"6773":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-91","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"It stops at a context that isolates the key again (an isolation boundary): the key is undeclared.","locale":"en"},"6774":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-92","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"The first fiber that declares the key decides. It returns the binding that fiber **committed** to when it loaded; a fiber that declares the key but has no committed binding yields `Inactive`.","locale":"en"},"6775":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-93","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"The root context, which cannot declare `inject`, has **unchecked** access to the live store, as in Cordis.","locale":"en"},"6776":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-94","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"Because checked access reads the committed view rather than the live store, a dependency stays readable while the consumer runs its own teardown, even if the provider is already gone from the store (Theorem 70 of the paper).","locale":"en"},"6777":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-95","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"The errors:","locale":"en"},"6778":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-96","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`AccessError`","locale":"en"},"6779":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-97","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"Message","locale":"en"},"6780":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-98","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`Undeclared { key }`","locale":"en"},"6781":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-99","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`cannot get property \"key\" without inject`","locale":"en"},"6782":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-100","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`Inactive { key }`","locale":"en"},"6783":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-101","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`cannot get required service \"key\" in inactive context`","locale":"en"},"6784":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-102","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`TypeMismatch { key, expected }`","locale":"en"},"6785":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-103","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#accessing","content":"`service \"key\" is not of type …`","locale":"en"},"6786":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-104","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#injected","content":"`Injected<D>` wraps a plugin context whose typed accesses are checked against its declared dependencies `D` at compile time. The `#[plugin]` macro reads `D` from the signature and generates both the declaration and the wrapper:","locale":"en"},"6787":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-105","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#injected","content":"`Injected::get::<S, _>()`: the `_` is the inferred position of `S` in `D` (`kardia_core::index::I0` … `I7`); you never write it.","locale":"en"},"6788":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-106","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#injected","content":"`Injected::deps()` returns all of `D` as a tuple of `Svc`s.","locale":"en"},"6789":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-107","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#injected","content":"`Injected::context()` returns the underlying, unchecked `Context`, and `Injected<D>` dereferences to it, so every other `Context` method is available.","locale":"en"},"6790":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-108","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#injected","content":"`#[plugin(name = \"…\", provide = [\"key\"], crate = path)]` takes an `async fn` whose first parameter is `Context` or `Injected<(..)>` and whose optional second parameter is `Arc<Config>`. It generates a plugin type named after the function in camel case (`greeter` → `Greeter`), with the hyphenated function name as plugin name unless `name` is given. Writing plugins is covered in Plugins.","locale":"en"},"6791":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-109","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"Every access returns a `Svc<T>`: the service value together with the **caller**, the context that accessed it. Cordis attributes calls with a JavaScript `Proxy`; kardia makes the caller an explicit part of the handle.","locale":"en"},"6792":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-110","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"Method","locale":"en"},"6793":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-111","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"Returns","locale":"en"},"6794":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-112","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"`*svc` (`Deref`)","locale":"en"},"6795":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-113","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"the service value","locale":"en"},"6796":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-114","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"`svc.caller()`","locale":"en"},"6797":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-115","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"the accessing `Context`","locale":"en"},"6798":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-116","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"`svc.key()`","locale":"en"},"6799":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-117","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"the key it was reached under","locale":"en"},"6800":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-118","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"`svc.impl_id()`","locale":"en"},"6801":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-119","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"the identity of the binding (never reused, so a replacement by an equal value is observable)","locale":"en"},"6802":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-120","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"`svc.arc()`","locale":"en"},"6803":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-121","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"the `Arc<T>`","locale":"en"},"6804":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-122","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"`svc.provider()`","locale":"en"},"6805":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-123","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"the providing fiber (the service's definition site)","locale":"en"},"6806":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-124","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"`svc.logger()`","locale":"en"},"6807":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-125","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"a logger for work done on the caller's behalf: named by the caller's `logger` interception `name`, else after the providing plugin","locale":"en"},"6808":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-126","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"`svc.intercepts()`","locale":"en"},"6809":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-127","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"the interception metadata of this access, outermost first","locale":"en"},"6810":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-128","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"`svc.meta()`","locale":"en"},"6811":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-129","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"that metadata merged with `S::merge_intercept`","locale":"en"},"6812":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-130","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"**Effects on the caller's behalf.** A service method that creates an effect for its caller registers it on `svc.caller()`. The effect then belongs to the caller's fiber and is reverted when the *caller* unloads, which is what Cordis's tracker achieves with `this.ctx`. Service crates expose such methods as **extension traits on `Svc<S>`**, which coherence allows because the trait is local. The timer service does this (simplified: the real `timeout` also reverts its effect once it has fired):","locale":"en"},"6813":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-131","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"So `timer.interval(..)` in `greeter` above stops when `greeter` unloads, not when the timer plugin does.","locale":"en"},"6814":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-132","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"**A service's own dependencies.** A service resolves its own dependencies through the `Context` it stored when it was constructed (its definition site), so no shadow contexts are needed. Two consequences differ from Cordis, where both follow the use site:","locale":"en"},"6815":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-133","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"Interception metadata of the outer caller does not reach the services a service calls in turn; it stays on `Svc::caller()`.","locale":"en"},"6816":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-134","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#svc","content":"Effects a service creates through its stored context belong to the service's fiber.","locale":"en"},"6817":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-135","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#interception","content":"Interception attaches metadata to a key along a context chain, so that a service can behave differently per caller (paper Def. 26–27). The usual example is the logger: `logger: { name: db, level: 3 }` renames and re-levels the logger of everything below.","locale":"en"},"6818":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-136","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#interception","content":"Where metadata comes from, outermost first:","locale":"en"},"6819":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-137","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#interception","content":"the metadata declared with the `inject` that admits the access (`Inject::with_meta`, or an entry's `inject: { key: meta }`);","locale":"en"},"6820":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-138","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#interception","content":"every `ctx.intercept(key, meta)` on the caller's derivation chain, outer to inner (a loader entry's `intercept` field adds one).","locale":"en"},"6821":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-139","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#interception","content":"`Svc::intercepts()` returns this list and `Svc::meta()` merges it with `S::merge_intercept`, by default `merge_shallow`: objects merged key by key, later values winning, like `Object.assign`. Override `merge_intercept` in your `Service` impl for another merge. On a context, `ctx.intercepts(key)` returns the chain's metadata and `ctx.intercept_meta::<T>(key)` merges and deserializes it (malformed metadata yields `T::default()`).","locale":"en"},"6822":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-140","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#interception","content":"Metadata also reaches availability predicates: `provide_checked` hands the predicate the consumer's metadata. The loader uses this for `inject: { loader: { await: true } }`, which makes `loader` available to an entry only once every entry has settled.","locale":"en"},"6823":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-141","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"Each key lives in a **realm**. By default all contexts share the key's root realm; isolating a key gives a context, and everything derived from it, a realm of its own:","locale":"en"},"6824":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-142","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"Method","locale":"en"},"6825":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-143","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"Derives a context in which","locale":"en"},"6826":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-144","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"`ctx.isolate(key)`","locale":"en"},"6827":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-145","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"`key` lives in a fresh, private realm","locale":"en"},"6828":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-146","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"`ctx.isolate_in(key, realm)`","locale":"en"},"6829":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-147","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"`key` lives in a given realm (`RealmId::new()`), shared by every context isolated into it","locale":"en"},"6830":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-148","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"`ctx.extend()`","locale":"en"},"6831":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-149","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"the context has its own mutable isolation and interception tables (an `Overlay`)","locale":"en"},"6832":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-150","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"`ctx.extend_with(&overlay)`","locale":"en"},"6833":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-151","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"the context is backed by an existing `Overlay`, shared with other contexts","locale":"en"},"6834":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-152","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"A provider binds in the realm its context resolves the key to, and a consumer sees only the binding of its own realm. Checked access stops at a context that isolates the key again, so an isolated subtree cannot reach the outer binding through an outer declaration. Related queries: `ctx.realm(key)`, `ctx.has_isolation(key)`, `ctx.isolated_keys()`; and for tooling, `ctx.bindings(key)` and `ctx.binding_provider(key, realm)`.","locale":"en"},"6835":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-153","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#isolation","content":"In configuration files, isolation is the entry field `isolate` (`{ db: true }` for a private realm, `{ db: shared }` for a realm shared under a label); see The loader.","locale":"en"},"6836":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-154","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"An event is a Rust type that implements `Event`. Listeners are registered per event type.","locale":"en"},"6837":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-155","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"`Output` is what each listener returns. `Bailable` decides whether a result stops a `bail` or `serial` dispatch, and whether it is a failure in `parallel`:","locale":"en"},"6838":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-156","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"`Output`","locale":"en"},"6839":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-157","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"Bails when","locale":"en"},"6840":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-158","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"Failure in `parallel`","locale":"en"},"6841":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-159","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"`()`","locale":"en"},"6842":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-160","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"never","locale":"en"},"6843":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-161","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"never","locale":"en"},"6844":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-162","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"`bool`","locale":"en"},"6845":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-163","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"`true`","locale":"en"},"6846":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-164","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"never","locale":"en"},"6847":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-165","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"`Option<T>`","locale":"en"},"6848":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-166","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"`Some(..)`","locale":"en"},"6849":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-167","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"never","locale":"en"},"6850":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-168","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"`Result<T, Error>`","locale":"en"},"6851":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-169","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"`Err(..)`, or `Ok(v)` when `v` bails","locale":"en"},"6852":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-170","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#events","content":"`Err(..)`","locale":"en"},"6853":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-171","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#listening","content":"Each registration is an effect of the current fiber, so a listener is removed when its plugin unloads. All return `Result<EffectHandle>`.","locale":"en"},"6854":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-172","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#listening","content":"Method","locale":"en"},"6855":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-173","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#listening","content":"Registers","locale":"en"},"6856":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-174","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#listening","content":"`ctx.on(f)`","locale":"en"},"6857":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-175","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#listening","content":"a synchronous listener, after those registered so far","locale":"en"},"6858":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-176","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#listening","content":"`ctx.on_prepend(f)`","locale":"en"},"6859":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-177","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#listening","content":"a synchronous listener, before those registered so far","locale":"en"},"6860":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-178","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#listening","content":"`ctx.on_async(f)`","locale":"en"},"6861":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-179","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#listening","content":"an asynchronous listener (returns a future)","locale":"en"},"6862":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-180","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#listening","content":"`ctx.once(f)`","locale":"en"},"6863":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-181","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#listening","content":"a listener that runs at most once, then removes itself","locale":"en"},"6864":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-182","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#listening","content":"`ctx.listener_count::<E>()` counts the current listeners.","locale":"en"},"6865":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-183","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"Method","locale":"en"},"6866":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-184","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"Behaviour","locale":"en"},"6867":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-185","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"`ctx.emit(&event)`","locale":"en"},"6868":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-186","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"calls every listener; asynchronous ones are started, not awaited","locale":"en"},"6869":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-187","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"`ctx.bail(&event)`","locale":"en"},"6870":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-188","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"calls synchronous listeners until one returns a bailing result, which it returns as `Some(..)`; asynchronous ones are started, not awaited","locale":"en"},"6871":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-189","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"`ctx.serial(&event).await`","locale":"en"},"6872":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-190","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"calls listeners one after another, awaiting each, until one bails: `Ok(Some(..))` with its result, or `Ok(None)`","locale":"en"},"6873":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-191","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"`ctx.parallel(&event).await`","locale":"en"},"6874":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-192","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"calls all listeners concurrently and collects failures and panics into an `AggregateError` (`one or more listeners of event E failed`)","locale":"en"},"6875":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-193","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"Dispatch takes a snapshot of the listeners and skips those removed meanwhile. An event can restrict its audience with `filter`, which gets the context each listener was registered in.","locale":"en"},"6876":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-194","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"A listener that panics, synchronous or asynchronous, never takes the dispatching code down with it:","locale":"en"},"6877":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-195","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"Mode","locale":"en"},"6878":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-196","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"A panicking listener","locale":"en"},"6879":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-197","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"`emit`","locale":"en"},"6880":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-198","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"is logged (`panicked: <message>`); the rest still run","locale":"en"},"6881":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-199","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"`bail`","locale":"en"},"6882":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-200","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"is logged and counts as not bailing; the rest still run. An asynchronous one, which `bail` only starts, is logged when it panics","locale":"en"},"6883":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-201","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"`serial`","locale":"en"},"6884":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-202","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"stops the dispatch: `serial` returns `Err(..)` with the panic, and later listeners do not run","locale":"en"},"6885":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-203","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"`parallel`","locale":"en"},"6886":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-204","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"is one of the failures in the `AggregateError`; the rest still run","locale":"en"},"6887":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-205","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"A listener's own `Err(..)` result is an answer, not a failure: it bails `bail` and `serial`, which return it as `Some(Err(..))`.","locale":"en"},"6888":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-206","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#dispatching","content":"Unlike Cordis, `emit` does not let a failing listener abort the dispatch, and there is no generic `waterfall`: extension points that Cordis builds on waterfall events are typed hooks (below).","locale":"en"},"6889":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-207","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"The runtime emits these from the root, after each state change:","locale":"en"},"6890":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-208","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"Event","locale":"en"},"6891":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-209","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"Fields","locale":"en"},"6892":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-210","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"Emitted when","locale":"en"},"6893":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-211","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"`PluginInserted`","locale":"en"},"6894":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-212","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"`fiber`","locale":"en"},"6895":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-213","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"a fiber is created (`internal/plugin` on insertion)","locale":"en"},"6896":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-214","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"`PluginRemoved`","locale":"en"},"6897":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-215","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"`fiber`","locale":"en"},"6898":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-216","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"a fiber is retired (`internal/plugin` on removal)","locale":"en"},"6899":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-217","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"`StatusChanged`","locale":"en"},"6900":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-218","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"`fiber`, `old`, `new`","locale":"en"},"6901":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-219","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"a fiber changes state","locale":"en"},"6902":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-220","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"`ServiceChanged`","locale":"en"},"6903":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-221","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"`key`, `realm`","locale":"en"},"6904":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-222","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"a binding of `key` in `realm` appears or disappears; delivered only to listeners whose context resolves `key` to that realm","locale":"en"},"6905":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-223","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"`ConfigCommitted`","locale":"en"},"6906":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-224","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"`fiber`, `config`","locale":"en"},"6907":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-225","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"a fiber's configuration is replaced through `update` (the loader's write-back point)","locale":"en"},"6908":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-226","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"`Replaced`","locale":"en"},"6909":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-227","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"`fiber`","locale":"en"},"6910":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-228","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#builtin-events","content":"a fiber is moved to another plugin implementation by `registry.replace`","locale":"en"},"6911":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-229","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#hooks","content":"Where Cordis uses waterfall events (`internal/config`, `internal/get`, `internal/update`), kardia has typed hooks. Each registration is an effect:","locale":"en"},"6912":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-230","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#hooks","content":"Hook","locale":"en"},"6913":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-231","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#hooks","content":"Purpose","locale":"en"},"6914":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-232","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#hooks","content":"`ctx.on_update::<C>(\\|config: &C\\| bool)`","locale":"en"},"6915":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-233","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#hooks","content":"offers configuration updates of the current fiber to the hook before restarting it; returning `true` takes the update over (no restart). The hook sees the decoded configuration and is skipped if `C` is not the plugin's configuration type.","locale":"en"},"6916":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-234","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#hooks","content":"`ctx.on_update_with::<C>(..)`","locale":"en"},"6917":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-235","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#hooks","content":"the same; a hook that takes the update over returns the future that `update` resolves with","locale":"en"},"6918":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-236","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#hooks","content":"`ctx.on_config(hook)`","locale":"en"},"6919":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-237","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#hooks","content":"a configuration resolution hook (`ConfigHook`) for every fiber of the root: it gets the source configuration and the next stage, ultimately the plugin's own decoding. The loader uses it to evaluate expressions.","locale":"en"},"6920":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-238","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#hooks","content":"See Revertible effects for how `update` uses these hooks, and The loader for the loader's own hook.","locale":"en"},"6921":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-239","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#logging","content":"The logger is part of the core. `ctx.logger()` returns a `Logger` bound to the current fiber:","locale":"en"},"6922":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-240","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#logging","content":"**Name:** the `name` of the context's `logger` interception metadata if there is one; otherwise the plugin name of the fiber (or of its nearest named ancestor, else `root`), hyphenated (`fooBar` → `foo-bar`, `snake_case` → `snake-case`).","locale":"en"},"6923":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-241","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#logging","content":"**Level:** the `level` of the `logger` interception metadata, if any. `logger.with_level(level)` sets it on a copy.","locale":"en"},"6924":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-242","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#logging","content":"`ctx.logger_named(name)` creates a logger with an explicit name (still taking the level from interception). `svc.logger()` logs on a caller's behalf (see above).","locale":"en"},"6925":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-243","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#logging","content":"Level","locale":"en"},"6926":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-244","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#logging","content":"Value","locale":"en"},"6927":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-245","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#logging","content":"`Level::Error`","locale":"en"},"6928":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-246","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#logging","content":"`0`","locale":"en"},"6929":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-247","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#logging","content":"`Level::Warn`","locale":"en"},"6930":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-248","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#logging","content":"`1`","locale":"en"},"6931":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-249","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#logging","content":"`Level::Info`","locale":"en"},"6932":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-250","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#logging","content":"`2`","locale":"en"},"6933":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-251","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#logging","content":"`Level::Debug`","locale":"en"},"6934":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-252","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#logging","content":"`3`","locale":"en"},"6935":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-253","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#logging","content":"Messages take any `impl Display`; format with `format_args!`. Exporters therefore receive finished text: there are no `%`-directives or custom formatters as in Cordis.","locale":"en"},"6936":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-254","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#exporters","content":"An `Exporter` receives every message:","locale":"en"},"6937":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-255","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#exporters","content":"`ctx.add_exporter(Arc::new(exporter))` registers it as an effect of the current fiber. A message reaches an exporter if its level is at most `exporter.level(name)`, else the logger's level, else `Info`. A `Message` carries `sn` (a sequence number shared by all exporters receiving the same call), `ts` (milliseconds since the Unix epoch), `name`, `level`, `text` and the `fiber` that logged it.","locale":"en"},"6938":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-256","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#exporters","content":"The root keeps a ring buffer of the most recent messages at or below the logger's level (1000 by default): `ctx.log_buffer()` returns them oldest first, and `ctx.set_log_buffer_size(n)` resizes it.","locale":"en"},"6939":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-257","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#exporters","content":"The terminal exporter lives in `kardia-logger-console`: register `ConsoleExporter::new(ConsoleConfig { .. })` directly, or load the `logger-console` plugin from a config file (its options are listed in Configuration).","locale":"en"},"6940":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-258","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#exporters","content":"There is no `tracing` bridge; the plan leaves a `tracing_subscriber::Layer` feeding exporters as an optional addition to `kardia-logger-console`.","locale":"en"},"6941":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-services-259","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-services#example","content":"A longer, runnable version also hot-replaces the database implementation:","locale":"en"},"6942":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","type":"page","content":"TypeScript and Tauri","breadcrumbs":["kardia Documentation","Guide"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","locale":"en"},"6943":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","content":"The @kardiajs npm packages: the same plugin model in TypeScript, the bridge that connects a TypeScript runtime, such as a Tauri webview, to a Rust kardia app, and extension points for Vue interfaces.","locale":"en"},"6944":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#model","content":"Two runtimes, one model","locale":"en"},"6945":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#core","content":"The TypeScript runtime","locale":"en"},"6946":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#bridge","content":"The bridge","locale":"en"},"6947":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#host","content":"Host: `kardia-bridge`","locale":"en"},"6948":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#client","content":"Client: `@kardiajs/bridge` and `@kardiajs/tauri`","locale":"en"},"6949":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#client-services","content":"Services from the client","locale":"en"},"6950":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#vue","content":"Vue interfaces","locale":"en"},"6951":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#responsibilities","content":"Where things belong","locale":"en"},"6952":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#protocol","content":"Protocol","locale":"en"},"6953":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-10","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","content":"kardia composes a Rust app. When part of the app is TypeScript, as in a Tauri app whose interface runs in a webview, the `@kardiajs` packages give that side the same model: plugins, services, revertible effects and lifecycle. The **bridge** connects the two runtimes.","locale":"en"},"6954":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","content":"Package","locale":"en"},"6955":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","content":"Contents","locale":"en"},"6956":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","content":"`@kardiajs/core`","locale":"en"},"6957":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-14","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","content":"Contexts, fibers, revertible effects, reactive services, events and logging. No dependencies; runs in browsers and Node.","locale":"en"},"6958":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-15","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","content":"`@kardiajs/timer`","locale":"en"},"6959":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-16","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","content":"`timeout`, `interval`, `sleep`, `throttle` and `debounce`, cancelled when their plugin stops","locale":"en"},"6960":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-17","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","content":"`@kardiajs/bridge`","locale":"en"},"6961":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","content":"The client side of the bridge","locale":"en"},"6962":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","content":"`@kardiajs/tauri`","locale":"en"},"6963":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","content":"The bridge's transport over one Tauri command and a `Channel`","locale":"en"},"6964":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-21","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","content":"`@kardiajs/vue`","locale":"en"},"6965":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-22","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","content":"Vue integration: contribution points, `<ExtensionSlot>`, composables, routes","locale":"en"},"6966":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","content":"`kardia-bridge` (crate)","locale":"en"},"6967":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-24","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","content":"The host side of the bridge, in the Rust app","locale":"en"},"6968":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-25","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#model","content":"Each runtime composes its own plugins. A Rust plugin cannot be a child of a TypeScript one or the reverse: an effect's inverse is a closure in one runtime's memory, and a service is a value there. So the bridge does not share a plugin tree. It keeps each side's view of the other in step:","locale":"en"},"6969":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-26","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#model","content":"**Effects never cross.** Each side reverts its own.","locale":"en"},"6970":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-27","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#model","content":"**Service availability crosses.** A service the host exposes appears on the client exactly while it is exposed, so a client plugin that injects it runs exactly then, and restarts when it is exposed anew.","locale":"en"},"6971":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-28","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#model","content":"**Calls are asynchronous** in both directions. A call into the other side fails with `unavailable` when that side is gone, and with `timeout` when it does not answer.","locale":"en"},"6972":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-29","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#model","content":"**Events** go from the host to every client, named.","locale":"en"},"6973":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-30","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#model","content":"This is the arrangement the paper describes for crossing a process boundary (each process hosts its own context, and calls between them follow an asynchronous contract, see Related work).","locale":"en"},"6974":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-31","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#core","content":"It is a port of Kardia's core rather than a wrapper of the TypeScript Cordis:","locale":"en"},"6975":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-32","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#core","content":"**Plugins** are functions, classes or objects with `apply`, each with optional `name`, `inject`, `provide` and `Config` (any Standard Schema validator). `apply` may return a promise, or a function that runs when the plugin stops.","locale":"en"},"6976":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-33","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#core","content":"**Services** are keyed by string. `ctx.get(key)` is checked access: it fails for a service the plugin did not declare. `ctx.live(key)` reads the live store without a check. A `Service` comes back as a view whose `caller` is the accessing context, Kardia's `Svc::caller`.","locale":"en"},"6977":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-34","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#core","content":"**Effects:** `ctx.effect(scope => ...)` collects inverses with `scope.defer` or returns one. An asynchronous body is never cancelled: `scope.checkpoint()` ends it once the effect is disposed.","locale":"en"},"6978":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-35","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#core","content":"**Lifecycle:** fibers move through `pending`, `loading`, `active`, `unloading`, `failed` and `disposed`, as in Rust. A plugin restarts when a dependency is replaced, waits when one leaves, and its provider keeps running until its consumers have cleaned up. `fiber.update(config)`, `restart()`, `ctx.onUpdate(...)` and `ctx.registry.replace(old, new)` (hot replacement, for Vite HMR) behave as in Rust.","locale":"en"},"6979":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-36","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#core","content":"**Events** are named: `ctx.on`, `emit`, `bail`, `serial`, `parallel`. The runtime reports `internal/plugin-inserted`, `internal/plugin-removed`, `internal/status`, `internal/service`, `internal/commit` and `internal/replace`.","locale":"en"},"6980":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-37","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#core","content":"**Isolation and interception:** `ctx.isolate(key, realm?)`, `ctx.intercept(key, meta)`, `ctx.interceptMeta(key)`.","locale":"en"},"6981":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-38","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#core","content":"Where it differs from Kardia and Cordis is listed on Implementation status.","locale":"en"},"6982":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-39","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#host","content":"The app creates a `Bridge`, mounts its plugin, and routes client requests into `Bridge::handle`. Plugins inject `bridge` and expose services; an exposure is an effect of the exposing plugin, so it is withdrawn when that plugin stops:","locale":"en"},"6983":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-40","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#host","content":"`Bridge::handle` runs its work on the runtime the bridge plugin runs on, so a Tauri command can call it from Tauri's runtime. The Tauri glue is one command (the `kardia-bridge` crate docs show it in full):","locale":"en"},"6984":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-41","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#host","content":"Call `bridge.close_client(label)` when a window is destroyed. A reloaded page needs nothing: its new session replaces the old one with the same label.","locale":"en"},"6985":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-42","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#client","content":"Host services appear as `host.<name>` and host events as `host/<name>` (the `prefix` option changes `host`).","locale":"en"},"6986":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-43","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#client","content":"The client connects in the background and reconnects when the host's bridge restarts. Its plugin is active while disconnected; host services are simply absent. `bridge.status` and the `bridge/status` event report `connecting`, `connected`, `disconnected` or `replaced` (another webview with the same label took over; it does not reconnect).","locale":"en"},"6987":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-44","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#client","content":"A failed call rejects with a `BridgeError` whose `type` is `unavailable`, `timeout`, `invalid` or `failed`.","locale":"en"},"6988":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-45","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#client-services","content":"A client can provide a service to the host, as an effect of the calling plugin:","locale":"en"},"6989":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-46","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#client-services","content":"The host sees it as a `RemoteService`, provided by the client's session fiber and withdrawn when the session ends:","locale":"en"},"6990":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-47","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#client-services","content":"A client can close at any time, and the Rust app usually runs without any window open. So a host plugin should look a client service up when it needs it (`live_as`), rather than declare it in `inject`, which would stop that plugin whenever the window closes. The client provides its services again after every reconnect.","locale":"en"},"6991":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-48","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#vue","content":"`@kardiajs/vue` lets extensions contribute to a Vue interface: components, views, settings sections, commands, routes. A contribution is an effect of the plugin that makes it, so it leaves when that plugin stops, and the interface follows.","locale":"en"},"6992":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-49","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#vue","content":"**Contribution points** are `Contributions<T>` services (`defineContributions(key)` provides one). `register(item)` is an effect of the calling plugin; items are ordered by `order`, an `id` is unique, and `items` / `entries` are Vue-reactive.","locale":"en"},"6993":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-50","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#vue","content":"**`<ExtensionSlot name>`** renders the components of a point, in order. Each one gets the context of the plugin that contributed it, so inside it `useContext()`, `usePlugin()` and `useService()` act as that plugin, and its effects stop with it. `props` go to every component, under each contribution's own; the default slot shows while there is nothing; the `item` slot (`{ item, owner }`) renders each contribution itself.","locale":"en"},"6994":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-51","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#vue","content":"**Failing contributions** are contained: a contribution that throws (in setup, render, a hook, a watcher or a handler) is replaced by the `error` slot (`{ error, item, owner, retry }`), or by nothing without one, while the other contributions keep rendering and the error does not reach the app. `retry()` mounts it again. `@error` (`{ error, item, owner }`) reports the failure, for example to show which plugin failed; without it, the failure is logged by the owner's logger. The owner's plugin keeps running: a broken view is one contribution of the plugin, and stopping the plugin would also remove its services and its other contributions. To stop it, call `owner.fiber.dispose()` from `@error`.","locale":"en"},"6995":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-52","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#vue","content":"**Composables:** `useContext()`; `usePlugin(plugin, config)` runs a plugin for the lifetime of a component; `useService(key)` is a ref that follows a service (`undefined` while none is provided); `useContributions(key)` is a computed list for custom rendering, such as a navigation menu; `useFiberState(fiber)` follows a fiber.","locale":"en"},"6996":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-53","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#vue","content":"**Routes:** `addRoute(ctx, router, route)` adds a vue-router route as an effect: it is removed when the plugin stops.","locale":"en"},"6997":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-54","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#vue","content":"**Rust-only extensions** cannot ship Vue code, but a Rust plugin can expose a value describing its UI (a settings schema, say) and a TypeScript plugin can register a generic component for it.","locale":"en"},"6998":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-55","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#vue","content":"Third-party UI code runs with the webview's full access to Tauri: load only trusted code into the main webview, and give untrusted extensions declarative contributions or a sandboxed webview.","locale":"en"},"6999":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-56","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#responsibilities","content":"Belongs to","locale":"en"},"7000":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-57","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#responsibilities","content":"Backend capabilities, state, settings, persistence","locale":"en"},"7001":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-58","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#responsibilities","content":"Rust plugins on kardia","locale":"en"},"7002":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-59","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#responsibilities","content":"Interface composition: settings sections, commands, renderers, panels","locale":"en"},"7003":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-60","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#responsibilities","content":"TypeScript plugins on `@kardiajs/core`","locale":"en"},"7004":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-61","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#responsibilities","content":"Which host services a client can see, and calls into them","locale":"en"},"7005":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-62","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#responsibilities","content":"the host's `expose`, through the bridge","locale":"en"},"7006":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-63","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#responsibilities","content":"Transport, window identity, permissions","locale":"en"},"7007":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-64","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#responsibilities","content":"Tauri (one command, one `Channel` per session, capabilities)","locale":"en"},"7008":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-65","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#responsibilities","content":"An extension can be Rust only (most backend capabilities; the interface renders what it exposes), TypeScript only (a panel or command using existing host services), or both: a Rust plugin that exposes a service, and a TypeScript plugin that injects `host.<name>`, so the interface half runs exactly while the backend half does.","locale":"en"},"7009":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript-66","page_id":"/en/docs/guide-typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide-typescript#protocol","content":"The protocol (version 1) is JSON, tagged by `type`, with camelCase fields; unknown fields are ignored. The `kardia-bridge` crate docs list every request and message. Any transport works: the bridge's end-to-end tests drive the Rust host over stdin and stdout (`crates/kardia-bridge/examples/stdio_host.rs`).","locale":"en"},"7010":{"id":"/en/docs/guide","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","type":"page","content":"Guide","breadcrumbs":["kardia Documentation","Guide"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide","locale":"en"},"7011":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide","content":"How to use kardia: config files, plugins, services, effects, the loader, hot reload and guest plugins.","locale":"en"},"7012":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide#which-page-do-i-need","content":"Which page do I need?","locale":"en"},"7013":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide","content":"The guide explains how to build apps with kardia, from the config file of the `kardia` binary to plugins written in Rust and guest plugins that reload in place. It assumes kardia is installed; Quick start shows a running app first.","locale":"en"},"7014":{"id":"/en/docs/guide-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide","content":"<Card title=\"The configuration file\" href=\"/docs/guide-configuration\" description=\"Entries and their fields, expressions, two-way sync, an