url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#fiber-state","content":"`LOADING`","locale":"en"},"7583":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-95","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#fiber-state","content":"`Reloading`","locale":"en"},"7584":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-96","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#fiber-state","content":"`ACTIVE`","locale":"en"},"7585":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-97","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#fiber-state","content":"`Active`","locale":"en"},"7586":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-98","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#fiber-state","content":"`UNLOADING`","locale":"en"},"7587":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-99","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#fiber-state","content":"`Unloading`","locale":"en"},"7588":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-100","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#fiber-state","content":"`FAILED`","locale":"en"},"7589":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-101","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#fiber-state","content":"`Inactive` + error outcome (§4.4 Failure)","locale":"en"},"7590":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-102","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#fiber-state","content":"`DISPOSED`","locale":"en"},"7591":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-103","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#fiber-state","content":"removed from the registry (uid `null`)","locale":"en"},"7592":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-104","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#fiber-state","content":"`_getState()` derives the settled state: `uid === null → DISPOSED`, `_error → FAILED`, `epoch !== INACTIVE → ACTIVE`, else `PENDING`.","locale":"en"},"7593":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-105","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#instantiation","content":"`fiber.ts:148-206`:","locale":"en"},"7594":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-106","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#instantiation","content":"A child fiber is therefore exactly Definition 52: an ordinary effect of the parent whose inverse retires it. Unloading a parent cascades to its children through the parent's accumulator. Unlike the calculus, retirement and removal are fused: the inverse retires, waits for the chain to finish, and then the fiber is gone (its uid is already `null`).","locale":"en"},"7595":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-107","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#target","content":"`fiber.ts:387-429`:","locale":"en"},"7596":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-108","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#target","content":"The epoch string is the paper's hash of `target(γ, n)`, plus the revision counter (a configuration revision is a new effect function, §4.4 Configuration; see Metatheory).","locale":"en"},"7597":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-109","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#state-machine","content":"`fiber.ts:431-514`.","locale":"en"},"7598":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-110","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#set-epoch","content":"Algorithm 5, `refresh`:","locale":"en"},"7599":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-111","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#set-epoch","content":"A change from one non-⊥ target to another while `ACTIVE` goes through `UNLOADING` and then chains into `LOADING` (unload checks the epoch at its end).","locale":"en"},"7600":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-112","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#reload","content":"**Inertia:** a stale target does not abort an in-flight `apply`. The load lands and the fiber unloads afterwards (async hosts take the *landing* alternative of L-Divert). The microtask yield before executing lets a burst of `update()` calls skip superseded loads entirely (`update.spec.ts: 'skips superseded loads before executing the plugin'`).","locale":"en"},"7601":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-113","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#update-state","content":"`fiber.ts:372-385`. It sets the new state, emits `internal/status(fiber, oldState)`, and **only on transitions into or out of `ACTIVE`** notifies the dependents of every provision still bound in the store (`ctx.isolate(name, impl.isolate).reflect.notify([name])`). Entering `UNLOADING` from `ACTIVE` therefore makes all consumers recompute an unsatisfied target *before* any inverse is scheduled (L-Leave), while the bindings are still physically present.","locale":"en"},"7602":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-114","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#guards","content":"**Fiber-level** (the `_unload` loop): a provider fiber does not run *any* disposer until no provision has dependents.","locale":"en"},"7603":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-115","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#guards","content":"**Binding-level** (`provide`'s inverse, see `provide`): withdrawing one binding waits for that binding's dependents only. This lets one provider withdraw binding A without waiting for consumers of binding B (`service-dispose.spec.ts: 'withdraws one binding without waiting for another binding from the same provider'`), and lets a binding be replaced during a consumer's initialization.","locale":"en"},"7604":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-116","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#guards","content":"Dependents are tracked as `Impl.dependents: Set<Fiber>` (populated at commit, cleared at the end of the dependent's unload), the runtime form of `relied_n`.","locale":"en"},"7605":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-117","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#await-update-restart","content":"`fiber.ts:516-552`.","locale":"en"},"7606":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-118","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#await-update-restart","content":"`await()` loops on `inertia` until settled, and throws `_error` if the fiber is `FAILED`.","locale":"en"},"7607":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-119","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#await-update-restart","content":"`restart()` (on `ctx.fiber`): `_revision++`, `_refresh()`, await. For the root fiber, `dispose()` *is* `restart()`: everything is unloaded and the root becomes active again.","locale":"en"},"7608":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-120","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#await-update-restart","content":"`update(config, noSave = false)` is the configuration revision path:","locale":"en"},"7609":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-121","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#await-update-restart","content":"resolve and validate the new config if loaded (the `internal/config` waterfall → Standard Schema `validate`, sync only; `ValidationError` keeps issue paths);","locale":"en"},"7610":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-122","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#await-update-restart","content":"`emit('internal/commit', fiber, config)` unless `noSave` (the loader writes the config back to its entry);","locale":"en"},"7611":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-123","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#await-update-restart","content":"store the config and clear `_error`;","locale":"en"},"7612":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-124","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#await-update-restart","content":"if loaded, `waterfall(fiber, 'internal/update', resolved, restart)`: per-fiber `internal/update` listeners (registered by the plugin via `ctx.on('internal/update', …)`) may accept the new config **without restarting** by not calling `next()`; otherwise `restart()`.","locale":"en"},"7613":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-125","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#await-update-restart","content":"The returned promise is marked handled, so dropped results do not cause unhandled rejections.","locale":"en"},"7614":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-126","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#await-update-restart","content":"Concurrency semantics verified by `tests/update.spec.ts`:","locale":"en"},"7615":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-127","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#await-update-restart","content":"concurrent updates settle on the latest config;","locale":"en"},"7616":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-128","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#await-update-restart","content":"updates during unloading coalesce;","locale":"en"},"7617":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-129","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#await-update-restart","content":"a superseded failure is cleaned up without failing the latest update;","locale":"en"},"7618":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-130","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#await-update-restart","content":"all waiting updates reject when the latest load fails;","locale":"en"},"7619":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-131","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#await-update-restart","content":"an outdated async generator stops advancing;","locale":"en"},"7620":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-132","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#await-update-restart","content":"a queued config is not loaded after disposal.","locale":"en"},"7621":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-133","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#failure","content":"From `tests/fiber.spec.ts`:","locale":"en"},"7622":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-134","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#failure","content":"A throwing `apply` → the error is logged, `_error` is set, the epoch becomes ⊥, partial effects are unwound via `_unload`, and the state is `FAILED`.","locale":"en"},"7623":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-135","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#failure","content":"A failed fiber **does not re-enter** on a dependency refresh (`_setEpoch` returns early). This matches §4.4: \"not retried against an unchanged environment\".","locale":"en"},"7624":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-136","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#failure","content":"`update()` (or `registry.replace`) clears the error and retries.","locale":"en"},"7625":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-137","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#failure","content":"Disposing a `PENDING` or `FAILED` fiber settles it to `DISPOSED`.","locale":"en"},"7626":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-138","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#nine-rules","content":"The rules are defined on Calculus.","locale":"en"},"7627":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-139","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#nine-rules","content":"Rule","locale":"en"},"7628":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-140","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#nine-rules","content":"Code","locale":"en"},"7629":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-141","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#nine-rules","content":"O-Insert","locale":"en"},"7630":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-142","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#nine-rules","content":"`parent.fiber.effect(() => { runtime.fibers.push(this); this._refresh() … })`","locale":"en"},"7631":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-143","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#nine-rules","content":"O-Retire","locale":"en"},"7632":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-144","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#nine-rules","content":"inverse of that effect: `uid = null; _setEpoch(INACTIVE)`","locale":"en"},"7633":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-145","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#nine-rules","content":"O-Remove","locale":"en"},"7634":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-146","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#nine-rules","content":"`_remove()`, runtime unregistered, state `DISPOSED` after the chain ends","locale":"en"},"7635":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-147","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#nine-rules","content":"L-Begin","locale":"en"},"7636":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-148","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#nine-rules","content":"`_setEpoch` → `_reload()` with state `LOADING`","locale":"en"},"7637":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-149","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#nine-rules","content":"L-Iter","locale":"en"},"7638":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-150","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#nine-rules","content":"async iterator loop in `_execute` while `epoch === oldEpoch`","locale":"en"},"7639":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-151","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#nine-rules","content":"L-Finish","locale":"en"},"7640":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-152","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#nine-rules","content":"`_reload` end with unchanged epoch → `ACTIVE`","locale":"en"},"7641":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-153","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#nine-rules","content":"L-Divert","locale":"en"},"7642":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-154","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#nine-rules","content":"epoch changed during load → iterator stops at next boundary, `_reload` chains into `_unload`","locale":"en"},"7643":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-155","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#nine-rules","content":"L-Leave","locale":"en"},"7644":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-156","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#nine-rules","content":"`_setEpoch` → `_unload()` with state `UNLOADING`; `_updateState` notifies consumers","locale":"en"},"7645":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-157","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#nine-rules","content":"L-Unload","locale":"en"},"7646":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers-158","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-fibers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-fibers#nine-rules","content":"`_unload` after the dependents guard","locale":"en"},"7647":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","type":"page","content":"HMR","breadcrumbs":["kardia Documentation","Cordis reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","locale":"en"},"7648":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-0","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","content":"How @cordisjs/plugin-hmr replaces changed plugins in place as one transaction, with union-find commit units, and how it differs from the paper's Algorithm 10.","locale":"en"},"7649":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-1","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"Integration","locale":"en"},"7650":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-2","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#module-graph","content":"Module graph","locale":"en"},"7651":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-3","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#reconcile","content":"`reconcile(callback)`: one transaction","locale":"en"},"7652":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-4","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#state-preservation","content":"State preservation","locale":"en"},"7653":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-5","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#watch","content":"Watch mode","locale":"en"},"7654":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-6","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#error-ts","content":"`error.ts`","locale":"en"},"7655":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-7","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"Paper vs. code","locale":"en"},"7656":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-8","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#node-specific","content":"What is Node-specific","locale":"en"},"7657":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-9","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","content":"This page covers `cordis/packages/hmr/src/index.ts` and `error.ts`, plus `core/src/registry.ts:185-209` and `core/src/fiber.ts:401-416` (see `registry.replace`). The paper counterpart is §5.2.2, Algorithms 8–10; see Implementation.","locale":"en"},"7658":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-10","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","content":"**The implementation differs substantially from the paper's Algorithm 10** (see Paper vs. code).","locale":"en"},"7659":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-11","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"`class Hmr extends Service`, service name `hmr`. Config:","locale":"en"},"7660":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-12","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"Key","locale":"en"},"7661":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-13","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"Default","locale":"en"},"7662":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-14","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"7663":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-15","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"`base?`","locale":"en"},"7664":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-16","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"`ctx.baseUrl`","locale":"en"},"7665":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-17","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"base directory","locale":"en"},"7666":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-18","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"`watch.enabled`","locale":"en"},"7667":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-19","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"`false`","locale":"en"},"7668":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-20","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"reload on file changes","locale":"en"},"7669":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-21","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"`watch.files`","locale":"en"},"7670":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-22","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"`['.', '!**/node_modules', '!**/.*']`","locale":"en"},"7671":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-23","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"glob filter","locale":"en"},"7672":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-24","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"`watch.debounce`","locale":"en"},"7673":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-25","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"100 ms","locale":"en"},"7674":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-26","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"debounce before reloading","locale":"en"},"7675":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-27","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"It requires Node's internal ESM loader (`loader-utils` → `ModuleLoader.fromInternal()`, which needs `--expose-internals` or the `node-addon-require-builtin` addon); the constructor throws otherwise (fiber FAILED, no service).","locale":"en"},"7676":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-28","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"Watching is an optional nested plugin `ctx.inject(['fs'], ...)`, active only while an `fs` service exists.","locale":"en"},"7677":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-29","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"`[Service.init]` records the **host modules**: the import closure of `process.argv[1]` (the main program, core, loader…), which can only change by restarting the process.","locale":"en"},"7678":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-30","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#integration","content":"There is no loader-specific code: the loader imports plugins through the same internal ESM loader, so their modules are in the cache hmr inspects. hmr replaces plugins at the **registry** level, and loader entries keep their fibers.","locale":"en"},"7679":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-31","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#module-graph","content":"hmr keeps **no graph of its own**. It reads the live graph from Node's ESM `loadCache` (`ModuleJob.linked`) and the CJS `require.cache` each time (`_edges`, `closure`). Builtins (`node:`) are skipped; native addons (`.node`) cannot be reloaded.","locale":"en"},"7680":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-32","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#reconcile","content":"`index.ts:309-699`. Transactions are serialized on a promise queue; re-entrant calls from inside a transaction (from the callback, or from a plugin `apply` during stage 3) are rejected using `AsyncLocalStorage`.","locale":"en"},"7681":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-33","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#reconcile","content":"**Roots**: `await callback()` → absolute paths (validated).","locale":"en"},"7682":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-34","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#reconcile","content":"**Sweep**: evict *failed* ModuleJobs from the cache (Node keeps them and rethrows on every import), per type slot.","locale":"en"},"7683":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-35","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#reconcile","content":"**Match**: loaded modules whose path has a root as an ancestor (whole-segment match). Host modules and native addons → `skippedHostModules` (reported only).","locale":"en"},"7684":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-36","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#reconcile","content":"**Analyze**: reverse edges (excluding edges from host modules). `accepted` = the changed modules plus everything that transitively imports them; `declined` = host ∪ the rest. *(The paper's Algorithm 8 is a fixed point over forward imports with cycles defaulting to declined; the code is a simpler reverse-reachability worklist.)*","locale":"en"},"7685":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-37","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#reconcile","content":"**Discover**: for accepted modules, unwrap the exports and keep those that are registered plugins; **group them by runtime** (several modules can export the same plugin).","locale":"en"},"7686":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-38","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#reconcile","content":"**Stale plugins**: per runtime, the closure of its exporters through accepted modules. The module to re-import is the **outermost exporter** (which keeps the entry module's `inject`/`Config` metadata).","locale":"en"},"7687":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-39","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#reconcile","content":"**Backup and evict** every evicted URL (the whole multi-slot ESM entry + the CJS module).","locale":"en"},"7688":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-40","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#reconcile","content":"**Stage 1, import**, sequentially per stale plugin: re-import and check that the exports are a valid plugin (`registry.resolve`). *All fallible validation happens here, while only the module cache has been mutated*, so later stages need no rollback. No cache entry is restored before every plugin has been imported.","locale":"en"},"7689":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-41","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#reconcile","content":"**Partition into units** with union-find: two attempts join a unit if their **old ∪ new** closures share an evicted module (two plugins sharing a changed dependency must not end up with different instances of it).","locale":"en"},"7690":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-42","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#reconcile","content":"**Abort/commit**: units with any failed import are aborted and their modules restored. Orphaned evicted modules are restored with the aborted units they overlap (unless they reach a committed unit). Stage-1-loaded modules linked against restored modules are evicted.","locale":"en"},"7691":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-43","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#reconcile","content":"**Stage 2, replace (synchronous)**: `ctx.registry.replace(oldPlugin, newPlugin)` per committed attempt. `replace` aliases the old plugin key to the new one (later `ctx.plugin(old)` instantiates the new code) and calls `fiber._replace(newRuntime, newInject)` on each fiber: re-check injections, clear errors, bump the revision ⇒ **the same fiber object unloads and reloads in place** (identity, parent, config and loader entry preserved).","locale":"en"},"7692":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-44","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#reconcile","content":"**Stage 3, settle (concurrent)**: `await Promise.all(fibers.map(f => f.await().catch(noop)))`. There is **no rollback**: a plugin whose new `apply` throws stays FAILED (as on a cold start) and is retried on the next change.","locale":"en"},"7693":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-45","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#reconcile","content":"The result is `{ settledFibers, importFailures: { urls, error }[], skippedHostModules }`.","locale":"en"},"7694":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-46","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#state-preservation","content":"Kept","locale":"en"},"7695":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-47","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#state-preservation","content":"Lost","locale":"en"},"7696":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-48","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#state-preservation","content":"fiber objects and uids, parents, configs, loader entries, services of *other* fibers","locale":"en"},"7697":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-49","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#state-preservation","content":"all effects of the old instance (disposed by the normal unload path, which waits for dependents first, so the new instance never overlaps the old one) and the module-level state of re-imported modules","locale":"en"},"7698":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-50","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#state-preservation","content":"Unrelated plugins are untouched. Different fibers reload concurrently (a slow drain does not delay a fast plugin).","locale":"en"},"7699":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-51","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#watch","content":"`index.ts:135-186`. `ctx.fs.watch(baseDir, { filter }).on('change', f => …)` → debounce → a serialized `flush` reconciling `retained ∪ stashed`.","locale":"en"},"7700":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-52","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#watch","content":"Host-module changes are warned about.","locale":"en"},"7701":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-53","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#watch","content":"Files of failed units are **retained** and retried together with the next change (a broken file and its dependency are retried together when only one of them is repaired).","locale":"en"},"7702":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-54","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#watch","content":"Only `change` events exist; a new file matters once a changed importer imports it.","locale":"en"},"7703":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-55","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#error-ts","content":"Pretty-prints esbuild `BuildFailure`s (tsx transpile errors) with `@babel/code-frame`.","locale":"en"},"7704":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-56","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"Aspect","locale":"en"},"7705":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-57","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"Paper (Algorithms 8–10)","locale":"en"},"7706":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-58","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"Code","locale":"en"},"7707":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-59","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"Classification","locale":"en"},"7708":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-60","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"forward fixed point; cycles default to declined","locale":"en"},"7709":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-61","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"reverse-reachability from changed modules; host modules declined","locale":"en"},"7710":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-62","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"Stale detection","locale":"en"},"7711":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-63","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"per *entry* (`entry.url`)","locale":"en"},"7712":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-64","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"per *plugin runtime* (any registered plugin exported by an accepted module); loader-agnostic","locale":"en"},"7713":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-65","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"Swap","locale":"en"},"7714":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-66","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"`entry.fiber.dispose(); entry.fiber ← ctx.use(import(url), config)`","locale":"en"},"7715":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-67","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"`registry.replace` → same fiber object reloads in place","locale":"en"},"7716":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-68","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"Failure handling","locale":"en"},"7717":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-69","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"restore caches and rebuild *every* stale entry from backup, rethrow","locale":"en"},"7718":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-70","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"validation in stage 1; failing **units** (union-find) aborted and restored, others committed; failures of the new `apply` stay FAILED (no rollback)","locale":"en"},"7719":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-71","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"Atomicity","locale":"en"},"7720":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-72","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"all-or-nothing","locale":"en"},"7721":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-73","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"per dependency-connected unit","locale":"en"},"7722":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-74","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"Re-entrancy","locale":"en"},"7723":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-75","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"not discussed","locale":"en"},"7724":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-76","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"serialized queue + AsyncLocalStorage rejection","locale":"en"},"7725":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-77","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#paper-vs-code","content":"The code's design is arguably stronger: commit/abort is per unit, and the \"point of no return\" is placed after the only fallible step that can be cleanly reverted.","locale":"en"},"7726":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr-78","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-hmr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-hmr#node-specific","content":"Everything in Module graph and steps 2, 7–8 and 10 of the transaction depend on Node's module caches and internals. The *algorithm* (match → accept → group by runtime → stage-1 validation → union-find units → replace in place → settle) is portable once a host-owned module registry exists. See Loader, include and HMR for kardia's design.","locale":"en"},"7727":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","type":"page","content":"Include and group","breadcrumbs":["kardia Documentation","Cordis reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-include","locale":"en"},"7728":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-0","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include","content":"How @cordisjs/plugin-include grafts a YAML/JSON file into the entry tree and keeps file and fibers in two-way sync, and what @cordisjs/plugin-group is.","locale":"en"},"7729":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-1","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-include#group","content":"Group","locale":"en"},"7730":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-2","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-include#include","content":"Include: a file-backed `EntryTree`","locale":"en"},"7731":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-3","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"State","locale":"en"},"7732":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-4","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-include#io-loop","content":"The IO loop","locale":"en"},"7733":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-5","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-include#read","content":"`_read()`","locale":"en"},"7734":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-6","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-include#write","content":"`_write()`","locale":"en"},"7735":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-7","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-include#apply","content":"Tree application","locale":"en"},"7736":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-8","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-include#journal","content":"Journal","locale":"en"},"7737":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-9","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-include#patches","content":"Patches","locale":"en"},"7738":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-10","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-include#source-locations","content":"Source locations","locale":"en"},"7739":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-11","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-include#errors","content":"Errors","locale":"en"},"7740":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-12","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-include#design-notes","content":"Design notes","locale":"en"},"7741":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-13","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include","content":"This page covers `cordis/packages/include/src/{index,journal,patch}.ts` and `packages/group/src/index.ts`. The paper counterpart is §5.2.1 (\"`@cordisjs/include` loads an external configuration file (YAML or JSON) and grafts its entries in as a nested subtree\", see Implementation). The paper does not describe the synchronization machinery below; it is an implementation contribution.","locale":"en"},"7742":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-14","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#group","content":"`packages/group/src/index.ts` only re-exports `Group` from the loader (see `EntryTree` and `EntryGroup`). Its config is the list of child entries; config updates are absorbed in place as a keyed diff.","locale":"en"},"7743":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-15","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#include","content":"`class Include extends EntryTree`, with `inject = ['loader']`, used as:","locale":"en"},"7744":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-16","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#include","content":"It is a class plugin whose async-generator `[Service.init]` reads the file, yields `() => this.stop()`, and applies the tree. Its entries' composite ids are `<includeEntryId>:<localId>`; includes nest.","locale":"en"},"7745":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-17","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#include","content":"`path` resolves against the parent tree's `baseUrl`; the include's own `ctx.baseUrl` becomes the file's directory (nested names and includes resolve relative to the file).","locale":"en"},"7746":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-18","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#include","content":"`initial` is written if the file does not exist (ENOENT only); an unparsable existing file is **never overwritten**.","locale":"en"},"7747":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-19","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#include","content":"`watch: true` → `ctx.inject(['fs'], ctx => ctx.fs.watch(filename).on('change', () => this.refresh()))`.","locale":"en"},"7748":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-20","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#include","content":"An `internal/update` listener reconfigures in place (new `patches`) unless `path`/`watch` changed (then it does a full restart).","locale":"en"},"7749":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-21","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"Field","locale":"en"},"7750":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-22","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"7751":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-23","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"`filename`","locale":"en"},"7752":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-24","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"the resolved file","locale":"en"},"7753":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-25","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"`type`","locale":"en"},"7754":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-26","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"`application/json` or `application/yaml`, by extension","locale":"en"},"7755":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-27","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"`cache?`","locale":"en"},"7756":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-28","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"`{ content, data (parsed, ids assigned, unpatched), syntax? }`","locale":"en"},"7757":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-29","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"`journal`","locale":"en"},"7758":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-30","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"`Map<id, JournalRecord>`: tree-side changes not yet in the file","locale":"en"},"7759":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-31","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"`index?`","locale":"en"},"7760":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-32","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"`PatchIndex` (ownership)","locale":"en"},"7761":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-33","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"`anonymous`","locale":"en"},"7762":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-34","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"ids invented for id-less file entries","locale":"en"},"7763":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-35","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"`dirtyRead` / `dirtyWrite`","locale":"en"},"7764":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-36","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"IO flags","locale":"en"},"7765":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-37","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"`_draining`","locale":"en"},"7766":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-38","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"the running IO loop","locale":"en"},"7767":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-39","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"`_pendingTree` / `_applyTask`","locale":"en"},"7768":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-40","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#state","content":"latest-wins application","locale":"en"},"7769":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-41","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#io-loop","content":"`index.ts:365-397`. A single-flight `_drain` runs `while (dirtyRead || dirtyWrite) { read-if-dirty; write-if-dirty }`. Read errors are **warnings** (half-written files are routine while editing) and stop the loop without writing (the file state is unknown); write errors are logged and the loop continues. `commit(change)` (from the tree) records into the journal, sets `dirtyWrite` and drains. `refresh()` (the watcher) sets `dirtyRead`.","locale":"en"},"7770":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-42","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#read","content":"Read; identical content ⇒ no-op (this also suppresses watcher feedback from its own writes).","locale":"en"},"7771":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-43","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#read","content":"Parse YAML (core schema regardless of `%YAML`, custom tag `!!js`, **errors and warnings both fatal**) or JSON; map issues to `file:line:col` (1-based, **UTF-16 columns**).","locale":"en"},"7772":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-44","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#read","content":"Validate the top-level array and the object entries; on failure keep the previous tree.","locale":"en"},"7773":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-45","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#read","content":"Assign ids to anonymous entries (stable across reads: the previous id is reused if the parent is the same and the options are deep-equal).","locale":"en"},"7774":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-46","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#read","content":"If this is not the first read: a three-way **reconcile** of the journal against the old and new file states; the **file wins** on conflict, and each conflict is logged.","locale":"en"},"7775":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-47","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#read","content":"Cache and schedule an apply; if the journal is non-empty, schedule a write.","locale":"en"},"7776":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-48","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#write","content":"Re-read; if the file changed externally, merge first.","locale":"en"},"7777":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-49","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#write","content":"Snapshot-and-swap the journal; `routeJournal` sends each change to its **owner**: the file data, a patch in the include's own config, or an entry embedded in a patch.","locale":"en"},"7778":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-50","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#write","content":"Patch changes are persisted by `this.ctx.fiber.update(newConfig)` (not awaited), which flows through `internal/commit` into the **parent** tree's file.","locale":"en"},"7779":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-51","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#write","content":"File changes are dumped (**whole-file regeneration: comments and formatting are lost**) and written atomically: a temp file `.<base>.<pid>.<seq>.tmp` in the same directory, a stale-content check before **every** rename attempt, and rename with retries on EACCES/EPERM/EBUSY (11 attempts, linear backoff).","locale":"en"},"7780":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-52","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#write","content":"Read-only files keep changes in memory, with a warning.","locale":"en"},"7781":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-53","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#apply","content":"`applyPatches(cache.data, patches)` (a fresh clone every time, so removing a patch reverts it) → `applyJournal(data, journal)` (overlay unwritten runtime changes) → latest-wins `root.update(tree)` → `EntryGroup` keyed reconciliation.","locale":"en"},"7782":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-54","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#journal","content":"`journal.ts` contains pure functions:","locale":"en"},"7783":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-55","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#journal","content":"Function","locale":"en"},"7784":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-56","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#journal","content":"Purpose","locale":"en"},"7785":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-57","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#journal","content":"`record`","locale":"en"},"7786":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-58","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#journal","content":"deltas captured at report time","locale":"en"},"7787":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-59","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#journal","content":"`mergeRecords`","locale":"en"},"7788":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-60","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#journal","content":"remove∘created-upsert = nothing; upsert after remove ⇒ `created:false`; changes merged newer-wins","locale":"en"},"7789":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-61","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#journal","content":"`flatten`, `applyChanges`, `detach`, `place`, `applyJournal`","locale":"en"},"7790":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-62","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#journal","content":"apply records to entry lists","locale":"en"},"7791":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-63","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#journal","content":"`reconcile(journal, base, theirs, fileOwned)`","locale":"en"},"7792":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-64","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#journal","content":"the three-way merge, where conflicting keys/moves/removals are dropped from the journal (\"file wins\")","locale":"en"},"7793":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-65","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#patches","content":"`patch.ts`:","locale":"en"},"7794":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-66","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#patches","content":"An **insert patch** `{ id?, insert: [...] }` appends entries into a group (or the root).","locale":"en"},"7795":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-67","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#patches","content":"An **override patch** `{ id, name?, ...keys }` overrides keys of an existing entry. `name`, if given, must match (a guard against patching a different plugin); overriding a group's `config` replaces its child list.","locale":"en"},"7796":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-68","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#patches","content":"`applyPatches` builds a `PatchIndex` recording the **owner** of every entry and key: `file`, `patch{index}` or `embedded{index, key}`. Later patches can address entries inserted by earlier ones.","locale":"en"},"7797":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-69","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#patches","content":"`routeJournal` writes each runtime edit back to its owner: patch-owned keys → the patch; entries inserted by a patch → inside the patch; the rest → the file.","locale":"en"},"7798":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-70","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#source-locations","content":"`_route(id, path)` finds where a value is written (file, patch, embedded) and delegates up through nested includes, producing virtual stack frames like `at a (inner.yml:1:3)` / `at inc (middle.yml:1:3)`. `walk` descends the YAML AST (resolving aliases to anchors); `seekExpr`/`scanScalar` map an offset inside an expression to a file offset (decoding quoted-scalar escapes).","locale":"en"},"7799":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-71","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#errors","content":"Error","locale":"en"},"7800":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-72","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#errors","content":"Side","locale":"en"},"7801":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-73","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#errors","content":"`ConfigFileError(stage: 'read'\\|'parse'\\|'validate', path, cause, issues[])`","locale":"en"},"7802":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-74","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#errors","content":"include","locale":"en"},"7803":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-75","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#errors","content":"`StaleWriteError`","locale":"en"},"7804":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-76","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#errors","content":"include (internal)","locale":"en"},"7805":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-77","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#errors","content":"`EntryValidationError`, `ModuleNotFoundError`, relocated `ValidationError`","locale":"en"},"7806":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-78","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#errors","content":"loader","locale":"en"},"7807":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-79","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#design-notes","content":"The include is the clearest example of the paper's *bidirectional* binding between configuration and fibers: runtime changes (plugin self-update or self-disable, API edits) flow back into files, file edits flow into fibers, and conflicts are resolved deterministically.","locale":"en"},"7808":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-80","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#design-notes","content":"Correctness relies on confluence (Theorem 80, see Metatheory): the include may apply intermediate trees, skip them (latest-wins) or apply them in a different order; the quiescent state depends only on the final tree.","locale":"en"},"7809":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-include-81","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-include","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-include#design-notes","content":"The synchronization core (journal, patch, reconcile, routing, id assignment) is **pure data transformation** over entry lists and is the most portable part of the code base.","locale":"en"},"7810":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","type":"page","content":"Loader","breadcrumbs":["kardia Documentation","Cordis reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-loader","locale":"en"},"7811":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-0","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader","content":"How @cordisjs/plugin-loader turns a declarative tree of entries into fibers and keeps both in step: entries, expressions, reconciliation, managed realms and validation.","locale":"en"},"7812":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-1","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#role","content":"Role","locale":"en"},"7813":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-2","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#data-model","content":"Data model","locale":"en"},"7814":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-3","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry-options","content":"`EntryOptions`","locale":"en"},"7815":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-4","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry","content":"`Entry`","locale":"en"},"7816":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-5","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#two-fibers","content":"Two fibers per entry when `inject` is set","locale":"en"},"7817":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-6","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#hooks","content":"Core hooks installed by the loader","locale":"en"},"7818":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-7","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#expressions","content":"Expressions","locale":"en"},"7819":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-8","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#algorithms","content":"Algorithms","locale":"en"},"7820":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-9","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry-update","content":"`Entry.update(options, create, force)`","locale":"en"},"7821":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-10","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#init","content":"`init` / `_init`: concurrency-safe (re)initialization","locale":"en"},"7822":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-11","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry-tree","content":"`EntryTree` and `EntryGroup`","locale":"en"},"7823":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-12","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#module-import","content":"Module import (Node-specific)","locale":"en"},"7824":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-13","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#managed-realms","content":"Managed realms","locale":"en"},"7825":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-14","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#validation","content":"Validation","locale":"en"},"7826":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-15","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#concurrency","content":"Concurrency model","locale":"en"},"7827":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-16","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader","content":"This page covers `cordis/packages/loader/src/**`. The paper counterparts are §5.2.1 *Declarative configuration* (see Implementation) and §4.4 *Configuration* (see Metatheory). File:line references on this page are relative to `packages/loader/src/`.","locale":"en"},"7828":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-17","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#role","content":"The loader turns a declarative **configuration tree** of *entries* into live fibers and keeps the two in step **bidirectionally**: config changes reconcile the fibers, and a plugin that updates its own config (`ctx.fiber.update`) or disposes itself (`ctx.fiber.dispose()`) is written back to its entry. It provides the `loader` service and owns the in-memory root tree; the same machinery is reused by `group` and `include` (see Include and group).","locale":"en"},"7829":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-18","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#role","content":"**Bootstrap** (`core/bin.js`): create a root `Context`, set `baseUrl` to the cwd, `await ctx.plugin(Loader)`, then `ctx.loader.create({ name: '@cordisjs/plugin-include', config: { path: './cordis.yml' } })`.","locale":"en"},"7830":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-19","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry-options","content":"`config/entry.ts:8-16`, plus `isolate` from `config/isolate.ts:6-9`:","locale":"en"},"7831":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-20","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry-options","content":"`null` means \"delete this key\" when merging; unknown keys are tolerated (only known keys are validated). `sortKeys` gives a stable order (`id`, `name`, the others alphabetically, `config` last) for file writes.","locale":"en"},"7832":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-21","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry-options","content":"Mapping to Definition 81: `id` ✔, `url` → `name`, `isolate` ✔, `intercept` ✔, `config` ✔, `disabled` ✔, plus `inject` and `group`, which the paper does not list.","locale":"en"},"7833":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-22","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry","content":"`config/entry.ts:55-68`:","locale":"en"},"7834":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-23","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry","content":"Field","locale":"en"},"7835":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-24","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"7836":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-25","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry","content":"`ctx`","locale":"en"},"7837":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-26","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry","content":"`loader.ctx.extend({[Entry.key]: this})`; its prototype is **re-pointed** to `parent.ctx` on every patch (live re-parenting when entries move)","locale":"en"},"7838":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-27","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry","content":"`outerFiber?`","locale":"en"},"7839":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-28","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry","content":"exists only when `inject` is non-empty: holds the entry's `inject` and parents the inner fiber","locale":"en"},"7840":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-29","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry","content":"`innerFiber?`","locale":"en"},"7841":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-30","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry","content":"the real plugin fiber","locale":"en"},"7842":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-31","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry","content":"`parent: EntryGroup`, `options`","locale":"en"},"7843":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-32","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry","content":"`options` is the **same object** as the element in `parent.data`","locale":"en"},"7844":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-33","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry","content":"`subgroup?`, `subtree?`","locale":"en"},"7845":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-34","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry","content":"set when the plugin constructs an `EntryGroup` (Group) or is an `EntryTree` (Include)","locale":"en"},"7846":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-35","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry","content":"`inject`","locale":"en"},"7847":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-36","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry","content":"resolved + evaluated inject","locale":"en"},"7848":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-37","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry","content":"`_initTask?`","locale":"en"},"7849":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-38","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry","content":"dedupe promise for (re)initialization","locale":"en"},"7850":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-39","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry","content":"`_disposing`","locale":"en"},"7851":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-40","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry","content":"marks loader-driven disposal (to tell it from self-dispose)","locale":"en"},"7852":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-41","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry","content":"`_verdict?: boolean`","locale":"en"},"7853":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-42","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry","content":"cached evaluation of `disabled` (`undefined` = undecided ⇒ disabled)","locale":"en"},"7854":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-43","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry","content":"`_intercept`","locale":"en"},"7855":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-44","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry","content":"live intercept table, mutated in place (`swap`) so running plugins see new metadata without restart","locale":"en"},"7856":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-45","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry","content":"`realm?`","locale":"en"},"7857":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-46","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry","content":"local realm (isolation)","locale":"en"},"7858":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-47","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#entry","content":"`id` is composite across include trees (`inc:mid:a`). `disabled` is `_verdict !== false || _parentDisabled()`; groups are never disabled themselves but pass their verdict to their children.","locale":"en"},"7859":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-48","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#two-fibers","content":"`config/entry.ts:36-46, 341-354`:","locale":"en"},"7860":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-49","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#two-fibers","content":"The **outer fiber** carries the entry-level dependencies; the **inner fiber** is the actual plugin. If a dependency disappears during the import, the async-iterator guard stops at the `yield` and the plugin never starts (an L-Divert at an iteration boundary). Losing a dependency later unloads the outer fiber, which disposes the inner one as a child effect; when the dependency returns, the outer fiber reloads and re-imports.","locale":"en"},"7861":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-50","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#hooks","content":"`index.ts:73-170`:","locale":"en"},"7862":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-51","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#hooks","content":"Hook","locale":"en"},"7863":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-52","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#hooks","content":"Purpose","locale":"en"},"7864":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-53","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#hooks","content":"`internal/config` (prepend)","locale":"en"},"7865":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-54","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#hooks","content":"relocate `ValidationError`s to config-file positions when the config came *from the file* (identity check)","locale":"en"},"7866":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-55","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#hooks","content":"`internal/config` (append)","locale":"en"},"7867":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-56","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#hooks","content":"**interpolate expressions** in `config` before validation (skipped for groups) in the inner fiber's context","locale":"en"},"7868":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-57","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#hooks","content":"`internal/commit`","locale":"en"},"7869":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-58","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#hooks","content":"plugin self-update: write `config` back into `entry.options` and `tree.commit(...)`","locale":"en"},"7870":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-59","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#hooks","content":"`internal/update` (global)","locale":"en"},"7871":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-60","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#hooks","content":"log `reload plugin`","locale":"en"},"7872":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-61","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#hooks","content":"`internal/status`","locale":"en"},"7873":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-loader-62","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-loader#hooks","content":"outer fiber → `UNLOADING