"page_id":"/en/docs/reference-paper-vs-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-paper-vs-code#defects","content":"`--mirror` flag parsed but unused.","locale":"en"},"8101":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-paper-vs-code-137","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-paper-vs-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-paper-vs-code#rust","content":"Follow the **code's** state machine (epoch with revision, inertia, two-level guard, `FAILED`, `DISPOSED`), because it is tested and handles configuration revisions; keep the paper's names in the docs.","locale":"en"},"8102":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-paper-vs-code-138","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-paper-vs-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-paper-vs-code#rust","content":"Follow the **paper** where the code is constrained by JS: make iteration boundaries explicit for all multi-step effects; detect dependency cycles at insertion time (cheap, since declarations are static).","locale":"en"},"8103":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-paper-vs-code-139","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-paper-vs-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-paper-vs-code#rust","content":"Replace Proxy-based caller attribution with explicit typed handles.","locale":"en"},"8104":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-paper-vs-code-140","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-paper-vs-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-paper-vs-code#rust","content":"Follow the **code's** HMR design (unit-wise commit, in-place replacement) over Algorithm 10.","locale":"en"},"8105":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-paper-vs-code-141","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-paper-vs-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-paper-vs-code#rust","content":"Fix the realm-GC early `return` in the port.","locale":"en"},"8106":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-paper-vs-code-142","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-paper-vs-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-paper-vs-code#rust","content":"How kardia carries these out is described in Lifecycle, API d