access, see Implementation) and §6.3 (capabilities, see Discussion and related work). The mechanism is mostly *implicit* in the paper, but it is essential for temporal composability in practice.","locale":"en"},"8115":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-services-7","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-services#problem","content":"A service is provided by one fiber (the provider) and called by many others (consumers). When a consumer calls, say, `ctx.timer.setTimeout(cb, 100)`, the timer it creates is an effect that must be **owned by the consumer's fiber**. Otherwise unloading the consumer would leak the timer, and unloading the provider would kill timers it does not conceptually own. Likewise, `ctx.logger('x')` should be named after the calling plugin. Cordis therefore distinguishes two contexts on every service call:","locale":"en"},"8116":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-services-8","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-services#problem","content":"Site","locale":"en"},"8117":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-services-9","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-services#problem","content":"What it is","locale":"en"},"8118":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-services-10","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-services#problem","content":"Governs","locale":"en"},"8119":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-services-11","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-services#problem","content":"**use site**","locale":"en"},"8120":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-services-12","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-services#problem","content":"the context the service was accessed from (the caller)","locale":"en"},"8121":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-services-13","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url"