/en/docs/reference-services#traceable-proxies","content":"`this.ctx.effect(...)` and `this.ctx.on(...)` are registered in the **caller's** fiber;","locale":"en"},"8153":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-services-45","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-services#traceable-proxies","content":"`this.ctx.otherService` is resolved against the **service's** own `inject` (the def site), even when called from root (`shadow.spec.ts: 'applies the service inject when entered from root'`);","locale":"en"},"8154":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-services-46","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-services#traceable-proxies","content":"`noShadow` services (events, logger, reflect, registry) expose the caller without preserving shadows.","locale":"en"},"8155":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-services-47","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-services#traceable-proxies","content":"`withProps` / `withProp` build lightweight proxies that override a few properties; `joinPrototype` merges a class prototype with `Function.prototype` for callable services; `createCallable` builds the function object.","locale":"en"},"8156":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-services-48","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-services#associated-properties","content":"Covered by `tests/associate.spec.ts`. A service named `foo.bar` (or a property provided as `foo.bar`) is reachable as `ctx.foo.bar`. Objects created by a service (e.g. a `Session` with tracker `associate: 'session'`) expose mixins registered under `session.*` by *other* plugins (`ctx.mixin('bar', { answer: 'session.answer' })`). Visibility follows the declaring fiber (`'associated access follows the service fiber'`).","locale":"en"},"8157":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-services-49","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-services#associated-properties","content":"This is how independent plugins extend each other's types at runtime: the dynamic counterpart of TypeScript module augmentation (paper §6.4, see Discussion and related work).","locale":"en"},"8158":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-services-50","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-services#port","content":"Concern","locale":"en"},"8159":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-services-51","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-services#port","content":"JS mechanism","locale":"en"},"8160":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-services-52","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-services#port","content":"Must be preserved as","locale":"en"},"8161":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-services-53","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-services#port","content":"Effects attributed to the caller","locale":"en"},"8162":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-services-54","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-services#port","content":"`service.ctx` returns use-site ctx via Proxy","locale":"en"},"8163":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-services-55","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-services#port","content":"service methods must receive/obtain the caller's context explicitly","locale":"en"},"8164":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-services-56","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-services#port","content":"Service resolution from def site","locale":"en"},"8165":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-services-57","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-services","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference-services#port","content":"shadow context in `locate`","locale":"en"},"8166":{"id":"/en/docs/reference-services-58","page_id":"/en/docs/reference-services","tags":[],