ed task, so dropping a `Disposal` does not cancel it. Await it to observe the result; `disposal.is_ready()` tells whether everything finished synchronously. Disposing an asynchronous effect whose setup is still running waits for the setup first."],[5889,"A `Disposer` is the inverse of an effect. It is consumed when it runs, so it runs at most once:"],[6663,"A `Failed` plugin recovers only through `update`, `restart` or a replacement."],[6234,"A `ModuleGraph` is also a `Resolver`, so the loader can resolve entry names through it; `Hmr::plugin(graph)` is the `hmr` plugin over the same graph:"],[5960,"a `PluginDef`"],[6640,"A `PluginDef` and a JSON configuration"],[6605,"A `PluginDef` is the type-erased form the runtime stores. You can build one from a closure:"],[7348,"a `Promise<function>`"],[6567,"A `serde::Serialize` value that also has a JSON view"],[6720,"a `Serialize` value that also has a **JSON view**, readable with `ctx.view(key)`, by loader expressions and by guest plugins. A `serde_json::Value` provided under a key (`provide_as`, `provide_arc_as`, `provide_checked`) is its own JSON view."],[5399,"A `Service` comes back from `ctx.get` as a view whose `caller` is the accessing context (Kardia's `Svc::caller`). Views are `Proxy` objects, so a service's `#private` fields do not pass through them; use `private`."],[6710,"a `Service` under `S::NAME`"],[6561,"A `Service` value under its key"],[6426,"A `TreeBackend` decides where a tree's changes go. Every method has a default:"],[4436,"A binding counts as available only while the installing fiber is `ACTIVE`; a provider entering `UNLOADING` stops providing, so dependents recompute an unsatisfied target and begin their own teardown *while its bindings are still in place*."],[6904,"a binding of `key` in `realm` appears or disappears; delivered only to listeners whose context resolves `key` to that realm"],[6771,"A binding that a fiber on the way provides itself, in the same realm, is returned directly."],[4167,"A calculus of dynamic composition"],[4816,"A calculus of dynamic composition"],[4207,"A calculus with realms would relax disjointness to \"disjoint within a realm\" (§4.4, see Metatheory). The single shared realm restricts components with a non-empty provision to one fiber at a time."],[6078,"A call fails with `the guest instance is disposed` once the providing fiber is gone, and with `invalid result of <key>.<method>: …` if the guest returns something that is not JSON. A guest calling back into an instance that is already running on the same thread (directly or through other guests) fails with `re-entrant call into a guest instance` instead of deadlocking. Like any service, a guest service is withdrawn when the guest's fiber is disposed."],[5625,"A Cargo workspace at the repository root, next to the untouched `cordis/` reference code (a local checkout of the TypeScript sources, ignored by git), `examples/`, `docs/` and the documentation site in `site/`:"],[7599,"A change from one non-⊥ target to another while `ACTIVE` goes through `UNLOADING` and then chains into `LOADING` (unload checks the epoch at its end)."],[4967,"A change to"],[6407,"a changed `name` or `inject`, or an entry that is not running: the entry is rebuilt (its fibers disposed, then started again);"],[6280,"A changed module does not load, or no longer exports a plugin"],[6513,"a char of an expression is located through YAML escapes;"],[6628,"A check or transform of the raw configuration before it is decoded"],[7594,"A child fiber is therefore exactly Definition 52: an ordinary effect of the parent whose inverse retires it. Unloading a parent cascades to its children through the parent's accumulator. Unlike the calculus, retirement and removal are fused: the inverse retires, waits for the chain to finish, and then the fiber is gone (its uid is already `null`)."],[7318,"a child plugin *inherits* the injection of an ancestor (`inject` declared on an ancestor admits access in descendants);"],[6990,"A client