e effect revertible."],[4479,"Temporal composability, global form (§4.3.2)"],[4837,"Term"],[4444,"Termination follows Theorem 73 (Metatheory): the provider graph is traversed on demand."],[5417,"Testing strategy"],[7089,"Testing strategy"],[7338,"Tests documenting the semantics"],[4897,"Tests run on a `current_thread` runtime with `tokio::time::pause()` for deterministic interleavings (the analogue of vitest fake timers); production may use the multi-threaded runtime. Testing describes which runtime each test suite uses today."],[5430,"Tests that depend on timers: the timer suite, and the core and loader tests whose effects wait on timers."],[4303,"That is, an effect function on the value plus an outcome. Its lift to `Σ` (eq. 31) reads and writes only the binding at `k`: typing confines the operation to its key. An operation that depends on another key must read that key's value into its argument. Operations induce an equivalence `≃_k` (§3.3.2, below)."],[6811,"that metadata merged with `S::merge_intercept`"],[6943,"The @kardiajs npm packages: the same plugin model in TypeScript, the bridge that connects a TypeScript runtime, such as a Tauri webview, to a Rust kardia app, and extension points for Vue interfaces."],[4348,"The **commuting part** of a computation is carried by effects: performed in any order, reverted in any order (Theorem 43). The **order-sensitive part** is carried by coeffects: within one component the accumulator imposes LIFO; across components a declared coeffect imposes \"provider before consumer\". Composability is therefore obtained at the grain of components, not of single effects."],[4368,"the **component loader**: configuration reconciliation and HMR (§5.2);"],[4367,"the **core library**: effect and coeffect systems (§5.1);"],[6310,"The **loader** (`kardia-loader`) keeps a tree of **entries** (a plugin name plus its configuration) in step with live fibers, in both directions: changes to the entries are reconciled into the running fibers, and